&lt;/div&gt;


&lt;p&gt;MIT licensed. Tested on Windows x64 (&lt;code&gt;Node v24.9.0&lt;/code&gt;, integrated webcam &lt;code&gt;USB\VID_13D3&amp;amp;PID_5415&lt;/code&gt; at &lt;code&gt;960×540 @ 30fps&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;@smartspectra/node-sdk@3.5.0&lt;/code&gt;). GitHub Actions CI runs all &lt;strong&gt;21 unit tests&lt;/strong&gt;, &lt;strong&gt;&lt;code&gt;verify-trace&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/strong&gt; (which asserts every sitting number reported in this post against committed &lt;a href="https://github.com/emarc99/presage-dev/blob/main/web/public/sample-trace.json" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;&lt;code&gt;web/public/sample-trace.json&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/a&gt; plus SDK privacy invariants), and the production Vite build on every push:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight shell"&gt;&lt;code&gt;git clone https://github.com/emarc99/presage-dev.git
&lt;span class="nb"&gt;cd&lt;/span&gt; presage-dev

npm install &lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;amp;&amp;amp;&lt;/span&gt; npm --prefix web install
cp .env.example .env      &lt;span class="c"&gt;# Add SMARTSPECTRA_API_KEY=...&lt;/span&gt;
npm run check             &lt;span class="c"&gt;# 21 unit tests + verify-trace + frontend build&lt;/span&gt;
npm start                 &lt;span class="c"&gt;# Starts localhost bridge &amp;amp; UI on http://127.0.0.1:4199&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;h2&gt;


  How It Responds to Human Signals
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Rather than piping raw SDK packets straight into React state, &lt;a href="https://github.com/emarc99/presage-dev/blob/main/bridge/signal-processor.mjs" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;&lt;code&gt;bridge/signal-processor.mjs&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/a&gt; transforms them into scale-invariant events. Every rule came from running it on my own laptop camera and watching what broke first.&lt;/p&gt;
