&lt;p&gt;Comparing the earlier Contact Sheets side-by-side makes each calibration step concrete—first Sitting 1 trapped in 100% cobalt &lt;code&gt;CENTER&lt;/code&gt;, then Sitting 2 unlocking multi-zone &lt;code&gt;L / C / R&lt;/code&gt; gaze (&lt;code&gt;91 / 235 / 40&lt;/code&gt;) while staying honest about two wavering breath plates (&lt;code&gt;1/3&lt;/code&gt; on Plates III–IV), before Sitting 3 in Demo above:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://media2.dev.to/dynamic/image/width=800%2Cheight=%2Cfit=scale-down%2Cgravity=auto%2Cformat=auto/https%3A%2F%2Fdev-to-uploads.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com%2Fuploads%2Farticles%2Fgwu2n6gdhalnyp12cod2.png" class="article-body-image-wrapper"&gt;&lt;img src="https://media2.dev.to/dynamic/image/width=800%2Cheight=%2Cfit=scale-down%2Cgravity=auto%2Cformat=auto/https%3A%2F%2Fdev-to-uploads.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com%2Fuploads%2Farticles%2Fgwu2n6gdhalnyp12cod2.png" alt="Sitting 1 Contact Sheet showing 151.4s sitting and 100% solid cobalt Center gaze bars across all five plates prior to additive iris+yaw fix" width="799" height="459"&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;br&gt;
&lt;em&gt;Sitting 1 (&lt;code&gt;151.4 s&lt;/code&gt;): Blinks and chest breath worked once past the startup freeze, but &lt;code&gt;0.7 * iris + 0.3 * yaw&lt;/code&gt; trapped &lt;code&gt;gazeScalar&lt;/code&gt; in &lt;code&gt;[0.486..0.493]&lt;/code&gt;—100% Center across all five plates.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://media2.dev.to/dynamic/image/width=800%2Cheight=%2Cfit=scale-down%2Cgravity=auto%2Cformat=auto/https%3A%2F%2Fdev-to-uploads.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com%2Fuploads%2Farticles%2F4qzdw88gzw8wg1j52uop.png" class="article-body-image-wrapper"&gt;&lt;img src="https://media2.dev.to/dynamic/image/width=800%2Cheight=%2Cfit=scale-down%2Cgravity=auto%2Cformat=auto/https%3A%2F%2Fdev-to-uploads.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com%2Fuploads%2Farticles%2F4qzdw88gzw8wg1j52uop.png" alt="Sitting 2 Contact Sheet showing 205.5s silent capture, 63% breath clarity, first multi-zone L/C/R bars, and honest 11/15 notes" width="799" height="459"&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;br&gt;
&lt;em&gt;Sitting 2 (&lt;code&gt;205.5 s&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;366&lt;/code&gt; silent keyframes): Additive iris+yaw (&lt;code&gt;0.95 / 0.55&lt;/code&gt;) unlocked Left/Center/Right bars (&lt;code&gt;91 / 235 / 40&lt;/code&gt;), Plates III–IV honestly read &lt;code&gt;1/3&lt;/code&gt; notes during unsteady breath beats (&lt;code&gt;11/15&lt;/code&gt; total), and &lt;code&gt;cardioMetrics&lt;/code&gt; stayed OFF.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;


  What Real Windows Runs Taught Me
&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;(Full technical log of all 10 hardware/SDK measurements: &lt;a href="https://github.com/emarc99/presage-dev/blob/main/docs/SDK-NOTES.md" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;&lt;code&gt;docs/SDK-NOTES.md&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/a&gt;.)&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ol&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Windows lied about the camera, and &lt;code&gt;checkDeviceReadiness()&lt;/code&gt; stalled for 30 s.&lt;/strong&gt; Windows MediaFoundation reports integrated laptop cameras (&lt;code&gt;USB\VID_13D3&amp;amp;PID_5415&lt;/code&gt;) with &lt;code&gt;facing="unknown"&lt;/code&gt; and &lt;code&gt;lensType="unknown"&lt;/code&gt;, so &lt;code&gt;CameraSelection.front&lt;/code&gt; fails immediately with &lt;code&gt;kInputUnavailable&lt;/code&gt;. Calling &lt;code&gt;sdk.checkDeviceReadiness()&lt;/code&gt; also tears down any active session and waits 30 seconds on &lt;code&gt;reference720p30('full')&lt;/code&gt;. Launching &lt;code&gt;CameraSelection.default&lt;/code&gt; directly at &lt;code&gt;960×540 @ 30fps&lt;/code&gt; locks at &lt;code&gt;29–31 Hz&lt;/code&gt; in ~7 seconds.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Landmarks arrived in raw pixels (&lt;code&gt;[316..564, 10..350]&lt;/code&gt;), not &lt;code&gt;[0..1]&lt;/code&gt;, so blinks and glances needed local geometry.&lt;/strong&gt; Unlike browser MediaPipe builds, &lt;code&gt;@smartspectra/node-sdk&lt;/code&gt; outputs all 478 landmarks (including iris centers &lt;code&gt;468&lt;/code&gt; and &lt;code&gt;473&lt;/code&gt;) in raw frame pixels—which also explains why &lt;a href="https://dev.to/timothy_akanbi/long-exposure-a-daguerreotype-that-takes-a-minute-because-the-sdk-does-113l"&gt;&lt;code&gt;timothy_akanbi&lt;/code&gt;'s &lt;em&gt;Long Exposure&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/a&gt; found raw blink flags and coordinates tricky for blinks. Dividing eyelid gap by eye-corner width puts open eyes cleanly at &lt;strong&gt;&lt;code&gt;ear ≈ 0.298–0.313&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/strong&gt; (&lt;code&gt;&amp;lt; 0.21&lt;/code&gt; closed) and triggering cuts &lt;strong&gt;on reopen&lt;/strong&gt; (&lt;code&gt;&amp;lt; 650 ms&lt;/code&gt;) avoids firing when someone closes their eyes (&lt;code&gt;≥ 1.1 s&lt;/code&gt;) to pause. Replacing &lt;code&gt;0.7 * iris + 0.3 * yaw&lt;/code&gt; with additive deviation around center (&lt;code&gt;0.5 + irisDelta * 0.95 + yawDelta * 0.55&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;&amp;lt; 0.455 / &amp;gt; 0.545&lt;/code&gt;) immediately turned Sitting 1's 100%-Center wall into mixed L/C/R gaze splits (&lt;strong&gt;&lt;code&gt;91 / 235 / 40&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/strong&gt; in Sitting 2; &lt;strong&gt;&lt;code&gt;171 / 406 / 93&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/strong&gt; in Sitting 3).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Auto-exposure collapsed brightness, dragging chest breathing across &lt;code&gt;[-6.842..+3.256]&lt;/code&gt;.&lt;/strong&gt; When USB camera drivers lack manual AE lock, SmartSpectra logs &lt;code&gt;mediafoundation_camera_source.cc:3019 [exposure-topup] lock collapsed image brightness (luma=18.8254 vs pre-lock 81.3485) ... exposure reverted to AUTO&lt;/code&gt;. That auto-exposure drift plus subtle posture lean sends &lt;code&gt;breathing.upperTrace&lt;/code&gt; sliding down a 10-unit ramp, and &lt;code&gt;upperTrace.stable&lt;/code&gt; stays &lt;code&gt;false&lt;/code&gt; for ~20 s waiting on &lt;code&gt;breathing.rate&lt;/code&gt;. Fitting a rolling &lt;code&gt;4.5 s&lt;/code&gt; &lt;strong&gt;Ordinary Least Squares (OLS) linear detrend&lt;/strong&gt; and scoring 2nd-difference curvature RMS directly responds within ~3 seconds while preserving &lt;code&gt;breathPhase&lt;/code&gt;.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;A 30 Hz status storm and a 1-frame startup flicker froze Sitting 1.&lt;/strong&gt; Like &lt;a href="https://dev.to/samarth_kumble_a91ad88634/practical-a-webcam-physiology-lab-that-grades-itself-against-a-wrist-count-3adp"&gt;&lt;code&gt;samarth_kumble&lt;/code&gt;'s &lt;em&gt;Practical&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/a&gt; noticed on Windows, &lt;code&gt;validationStatus&lt;/code&gt; fires on every single video frame (~25–30×/sec) even while &lt;code&gt;kOk&lt;/code&gt; never changes—and calling &lt;code&gt;SmartSpectraSDK.availableCameras()&lt;/code&gt; inside the status builder triggered &lt;strong&gt;30 MediaFoundation enumerations/sec&lt;/strong&gt; alongside 60 Hz SVG blur renders, while one stray &lt;code&gt;face.talking: true&lt;/code&gt; packet froze breath warmup at &lt;code&gt;55%&lt;/code&gt; and downward laptop angles read &lt;code&gt;SAD: 64.1%–97.6%&lt;/code&gt; at rest. Caching cameras, deduplicating &lt;code&gt;(validation, validationHint)&lt;/code&gt;, throttling UI updates to &lt;code&gt;~12.5 Hz&lt;/code&gt;, gating talking on &lt;code&gt;5&lt;/code&gt; consecutive frames, and smoothing &lt;code&gt;heavy&lt;/code&gt; at &lt;code&gt;≥ 86%&lt;/code&gt; cured all three.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Recording my demo sitting caught one more bug (the 42 ms eyelid-descent race)—and proved the talking guard and pulse gate live.&lt;/strong&gt; Speaking on camera across &lt;strong&gt;Sitting 3&lt;/strong&gt; proved the speech guard end-to-end: across &lt;strong&gt;&lt;code&gt;15&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/strong&gt; speaking episodes (&lt;code&gt;822&lt;/code&gt; talking packets at &lt;code&gt;29.5 fps&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;57&lt;/code&gt; keyframes in &lt;code&gt;sample-trace.json&lt;/code&gt;), &lt;code&gt;breathSteadiness&lt;/code&gt; stayed locked across &lt;strong&gt;&lt;code&gt;807 / 807&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/strong&gt; consecutive talking checks with &lt;strong&gt;&lt;code&gt;0&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/strong&gt; violations. Opt-in &lt;code&gt;cardioMetrics&lt;/code&gt; also behaved honestly once flipped ON mid-sitting (&lt;code&gt;dt = 264.6 s&lt;/code&gt;): Plates II–IV printed &lt;strong&gt;&lt;code&gt;71.8 / 77.1 / 77.2 bpm&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/strong&gt; (&lt;code&gt;75.4 bpm&lt;/code&gt; avg), while Plate I (pre-toggle) and Plate V (extreme left gaze pushing rPPG confidence &lt;code&gt;&amp;lt; 40%&lt;/code&gt;) stayed suppressed (&lt;code&gt;null&lt;/code&gt;). Out of &lt;code&gt;4&lt;/code&gt; long-blink pauses (&lt;code&gt;157.86 s&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;259.14 s&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;291.11 s&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;320.69 s&lt;/code&gt;), pause #3 exposed one subtle race: native &lt;code&gt;face.blinking&lt;/code&gt; fired at &lt;code&gt;dt = 289.947 s&lt;/code&gt; (&lt;code&gt;ear = 0.213&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;0.003&lt;/code&gt; above the &lt;code&gt;0.21&lt;/code&gt; closure cutoff) &lt;strong&gt;42 ms before&lt;/strong&gt; &lt;code&gt;ear&lt;/code&gt; dropped to &lt;code&gt;0.175&lt;/code&gt; at &lt;code&gt;289.989 s&lt;/code&gt; for a &lt;code&gt;2.44 s&lt;/code&gt; hold. Gating native &lt;code&gt;face.blinking&lt;/code&gt; fallback on &lt;code&gt;lastEar &amp;gt;= 0.25&lt;/code&gt; (&lt;code&gt;nativeBlinkEarFloor&lt;/code&gt;) eliminates descent misfires without breaking partial-blink fallback, locked in by &lt;strong&gt;Regression Test #21&lt;/strong&gt;.
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ol&gt;
&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight javascript"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="c1"&gt;// Excerpt from bridge/signal-processor.mjs — native blinking descent guard (Test #21)&lt;/span&gt;
