&lt;h3 id="agent-session-1410-17-two-things-to-catch-right-now-honest-audit"&gt;Two Things to Catch Right Now (Honest Audit)&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;ol&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Gaze bar is 100% &lt;code&gt;CENTER&lt;/code&gt; (solid blue) across all 5 plates&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Either you kept your head/eyes centered during the sitting, &lt;strong&gt;or&lt;/strong&gt; our gaze deadband (&lt;code&gt;&amp;lt; 0.41&lt;/code&gt; / &lt;code&gt;&amp;gt; 0.59&lt;/code&gt; in &lt;code&gt;signal-processor.mjs&lt;/code&gt;) is too wide for natural glances across a laptop screen (which typically only nudge &lt;code&gt;gazeScalar&lt;/code&gt; &lt;code&gt;±0.05–0.07&lt;/code&gt; without turning your whole head).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Check:&lt;/strong&gt; Did you try looking left/right and it wouldn't switch out of &lt;code&gt;CENTER&lt;/code&gt;, or did you just stay centered? If it felt stiff, I can tighten the trigger to &lt;strong&gt;&lt;code&gt;0.45 / 0.55&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/strong&gt; (with &lt;code&gt;0.475 / 0.525&lt;/code&gt; return hysteresis) so glancing at the left/right panes switches effortlessly and paints real L / C / R bars on the Contact Sheet.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;code&gt;web/public/sample-trace.json&lt;/code&gt; is still the synthetic placeholder (&lt;code&gt;sample_preview&lt;/code&gt;, 24 frames)&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;No file was written in &lt;code&gt;recordings/&lt;/code&gt; yet, which means &lt;strong&gt;&lt;code&gt;Record Sitting&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/strong&gt; wasn't clicked before entering Scene I on this run.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;To replace &lt;code&gt;sample-trace.json&lt;/code&gt; with your real sitting for judges on Vercel:

&lt;ol&gt;
&lt;li&gt;On &lt;code&gt;/calibrate&lt;/code&gt;, click &lt;strong&gt;&lt;code&gt;Record Sitting&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/strong&gt; (confirm the button switches to &lt;strong&gt;&lt;code&gt;Stop &amp;amp; Save Sample (N)&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Click &lt;strong&gt;&lt;code&gt;Enter Scene I →&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;, complete Scenes I–V.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;On &lt;code&gt;/contact-sheet&lt;/code&gt;, click &lt;strong&gt;&lt;code&gt;Save Recording → sample-trace.json&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/strong&gt; in the banner at the top.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ol&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ol&gt;
