                    &lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;No issue at all—every single one of those lines is harmless upstream C++ stderr output from inside &lt;code&gt;@smartspectra/node-sdk&lt;/code&gt;, not an error in AFTERIMAGE:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ol&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;&lt;code&gt;inference_feedback_manager.cc:114&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/strong&gt; &amp;amp; &lt;strong&gt;&lt;code&gt;absl::InitializeLog()&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/strong&gt; — Standard TensorFlow Lite / MediaPipe startup noise inside Presage's native addon whenever an SDK session starts (it printed twice in your second run because you started/restarted capture twice: timestamps &lt;code&gt;...4237&lt;/code&gt; and &lt;code&gt;...4520&lt;/code&gt;). Completely normal.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;&lt;code&gt;landmark_projection_calculator.cc:78&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/strong&gt; — Standard internal MediaPipe FaceMesh graph warning inside the native SDK; cannot be silenced from JS and has zero effect on tracking.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;&lt;code&gt;mediafoundation_camera_source.cc:3019 [exposure-topup] ... exposure reverted to AUTO&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/strong&gt; — Hardware-specific safe fallback on your integrated laptop camera driver:

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;SmartSpectra tries to lock Auto-Exposure (AE) at startup; your laptop USB webcam driver has no manual gain/AE lock, so brightness collapsed (&lt;code&gt;luma 81.3 → 18.8&lt;/code&gt;) and the SDK automatically recovered by reverting to &lt;code&gt;AUTO&lt;/code&gt;.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Zero problem for blinks, gaze, or chest breathing&lt;/strong&gt; (and our OLS linear detrending in &lt;code&gt;signal-processor.mjs&lt;/code&gt; already absorbs slow auto-exposure drift).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Good engineering note for your DEV post:&lt;/strong&gt; Because laptop webcams without AE lock make rPPG pulse noisier, this hardware behavior actually &lt;em&gt;validates&lt;/em&gt; why AFTERIMAGE builds core interaction on face + chest breathing and keeps &lt;code&gt;cardioMetrics&lt;/code&gt; opt-in &amp;amp; confidence-gated (&lt;code&gt;&amp;gt;= 40%&lt;/code&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ol&gt;



