&lt;h3 id="agent-session-1410-25-1-critical-factual-mistake-caught-in-our-draft--ui-presage-74"&gt;1. Critical Factual Mistake Caught in Our Draft &amp;amp; UI (Presage §7.4)&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Our current draft (&lt;code&gt;dev_submission_draft.md&lt;/code&gt;) and &lt;code&gt;CalibratePage.tsx&lt;/code&gt; claim:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;blockquote&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;"Leaving &lt;code&gt;cardioMetrics&lt;/code&gt; OFF avoids triggering Presage's automatic Presage → Anthropic LLM Insights cloud pipeline described in §7.4 of Presage's Telemetry &amp;amp; Privacy policy."&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/blockquote&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;That claim is contradicted by Presage's own documentation and SDK source:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;
- Presage's live &lt;a href="https://smartspectra.presagetech.com/docs/llm-insights" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;LLM Insights documentation&lt;/a&gt; states:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;blockquote&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;"Auto-fired vitals — once a session is running, the SDK automatically dispatches vitals snapshots of the accumulated metrics buffer: one the first time pulse rate has a stable reading, **one when breathing rate does&lt;/em&gt;&lt;em&gt;, one when HRV does, and then **one every 60 seconds for as long as the session runs.&lt;/em&gt;* ... The buffered metric values — an allowlisted subset of the computed metrics (&lt;strong&gt;pulse rate, heart-rate variability, and breathing rate&lt;/strong&gt;) as a columnar series."*&lt;br&gt;
- Presage Privacy Policy &lt;strong&gt;§7.4&lt;/strong&gt; states:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;em&gt;"Insights are generated automatically during SDK sessions and cannot currently be turned off by Developers or End Users."&lt;/em&gt;&lt;br&gt;
- And in &lt;code&gt;node_modules/@smartspectra/node-sdk/js/smartspectra.js&lt;/code&gt; (lines 386–398), the Node SDK &lt;strong&gt;unconditionally registers &lt;code&gt;onInsight&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/strong&gt; on every session. Because AFTERIMAGE requests &lt;code&gt;breathingMetrics&lt;/code&gt; by default (emitting &lt;code&gt;308&lt;/code&gt; &lt;code&gt;breathing.rate&lt;/code&gt; readings in &lt;code&gt;sample-trace.json&lt;/code&gt;), we &lt;strong&gt;cannot&lt;/strong&gt; truthfully claim that leaving &lt;code&gt;cardioMetrics&lt;/code&gt; off guarantees nothing hits Presage's §7.4 Anthropic pipeline without a packet capture proving it.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/blockquote&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Compare how two top &lt;code&gt;#presagechallenge&lt;/code&gt; competitors handled this exact fact:&lt;br&gt;
- &lt;strong&gt;&lt;a href="https://dev.to/emediongrgb/witness-camera-vitals-that-show-their-work-1b73"&gt;Witness&lt;/a&gt;:&lt;/strong&gt; Read the SDK 3.5.0 source, noticed it always registers an insight sink, and stated plainly: &lt;em&gt;"Until then I state what the code shows, not what I observed on the wire."&lt;/em&gt;&lt;br&gt;
- &lt;strong&gt;&lt;a href="https://dev.to/iszee23/senti-draw-the-tension-you-planned-see-the-tension-your-player-felt-1261"&gt;Senti&lt;/a&gt;:&lt;/strong&gt; Disclosed cleanly: &lt;em&gt;"Per Presage's documentation, it may also send short derived number summaries (never video) for an LLM wellness feature that apps cannot switch off. Senti does not request, show or store those insights."&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Because Presage engineers participate directly in final judging, leaving an inaccurate §7.4 guarantee in our Consent section is a serious vulnerability.&lt;/p&gt;


&lt;h3 id="agent-session-1410-25-2-what-the-100-entry-field-actually-looks-like-today-nov-22"&gt;2. What the 100+ Entry Field Actually Looks Like Today (Nov 22)&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Yesterday there were ~30 entries. Today there are &lt;strong&gt;100+ &lt;code&gt;#presagechallenge&lt;/code&gt; submissions&lt;/strong&gt; competing for &lt;strong&gt;10 total prizes&lt;/strong&gt; (4 Overall, 3 Most Creative, 3 Best Thoughtful Real-World). Your real competition now includes:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Creative / Experimental Track (your real lane):&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;
