&lt;h2 id="agent-session-1410-1-4-technical-feasibility-audit-smartspectranode-sdk350--model-cards"&gt;4. Technical Feasibility Audit (&lt;code&gt;@smartspectra/node-sdk@3.5.0&lt;/code&gt; &amp;amp; Model Cards)&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Checked directly against the published &lt;code&gt;@smartspectra/node-sdk@3.5.0&lt;/code&gt; package source, &lt;a href="https://smartspectra.presagetech.com/docs/nodejs" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;Node.js Docs&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href="https://smartspectra.presagetech.com/docs/data-types" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;Data Types&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href="https://smartspectra.presagetech.com/docs/measurement-quality" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;Getting a Good Measurement&lt;/a&gt;, the Nov 6, 2026 Model Cards, and live field reports from GitHub issues &amp;amp; &lt;code&gt;#presagechallenge&lt;/code&gt; builders.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3 id="agent-session-1410-1-platform--electron-pipeline-win32-x64"&gt;Platform &amp;amp; Electron Pipeline (&lt;code&gt;win32-x64&lt;/code&gt;)&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Built-in laptop webcam works in Electron (good news, plan note outdated):&lt;/strong&gt; Unlike the experimental C++ Windows SDK (&lt;code&gt;docs/cpp/windows&lt;/code&gt;), &lt;code&gt;@smartspectra/node-sdk&lt;/code&gt; &lt;code&gt;3.5.0&lt;/code&gt; &lt;strong&gt;officially supports &lt;code&gt;win32-x64&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;, because &lt;code&gt;@smartspectra/node-sdk/renderer&lt;/code&gt; captures via Chromium &lt;code&gt;getUserMedia&lt;/code&gt; → &lt;code&gt;MediaStreamTrackProcessor&lt;/code&gt; → &lt;code&gt;OffscreenCanvas&lt;/code&gt; → IPC &lt;code&gt;MessagePort&lt;/code&gt; → &lt;code&gt;useCustomInput()&lt;/code&gt; / &lt;code&gt;sendFrame()&lt;/code&gt;.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Hidden 720p CPU/IPC Bottleneck (&lt;code&gt;kSustainedLowFrameRate&lt;/code&gt;, code 14):&lt;/strong&gt; By default, &lt;code&gt;@smartspectra/node-sdk/renderer&lt;/code&gt; acquires &lt;strong&gt;1280×720 @ 30 fps&lt;/strong&gt;. Because Electron's &lt;code&gt;MessagePortMain&lt;/code&gt; drops &lt;code&gt;ArrayBuffer&lt;/code&gt; transfer lists (&lt;code&gt;js/preload/index.js&lt;/code&gt;), the renderer clones &lt;code&gt;~3.68 MB/frame&lt;/code&gt; (&lt;code&gt;~110 MB/s&lt;/code&gt;) after synchronous &lt;code&gt;ctx.getImageData()&lt;/code&gt; readback. In SDK &lt;code&gt;3.5.0&lt;/code&gt;, sustained low FPS &lt;strong&gt;terminates the session&lt;/strong&gt; with &lt;code&gt;kSustainedLowFrameRate (14)&lt;/code&gt; (&lt;code&gt;retryable: true&lt;/code&gt;). Real Windows/laptop builders (&lt;code&gt;Hear Me&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;Don't Blink&lt;/code&gt;) hit processing drops at 720p while rendering Canvas + screen-recording; dropping capture to &lt;code&gt;640×480&lt;/code&gt; or &lt;code&gt;640×360 @ 30 fps&lt;/code&gt; via &lt;code&gt;sdk.useMediaStream(stream)&lt;/code&gt; fixes this.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Virtual Webcam Trap:&lt;/strong&gt; &lt;code&gt;getUserMedia({ facingMode: 'user' })&lt;/code&gt; can select OBS Virtual Camera / DroidCam first if installed. Enumerate cameras and let the user pick.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;No Error Recovery Loop in &lt;code&gt;HUSH_PLAN.md&lt;/code&gt;:&lt;/strong&gt; GitHub Issue #18 (&lt;code&gt;Status code: 0&lt;/code&gt; / &lt;code&gt;kNetworkError = 5&lt;/code&gt;) and field logs (&lt;code&gt;kProcessingFailed = 8&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;kTimestampGap = 11&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;kSustainedLowFrameRate = 14&lt;/code&gt;) show transient dropouts happen mid-session. You need bounded &lt;code&gt;reset()&lt;/code&gt;/restart recovery.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Windows Packaging Caveat:&lt;/strong&gt; Presage's bundled DLLs in &lt;code&gt;@smartspectra/node-sdk-win32-x64&lt;/code&gt; are unsigned; Windows Smart App Control blocks unsigned packaged &lt;code&gt;.exe&lt;/code&gt;s (&lt;code&gt;Ghost Hunt&lt;/code&gt; hit this). Source-run (&lt;code&gt;npm start&lt;/code&gt;) should remain the primary judge path. Also note &lt;code&gt;ELECTRON_RUN_AS_NODE=1&lt;/code&gt; in VS Code terminals crashes Electron immediately unless unset.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3 id="agent-session-1410-1-signal-by-signal-audit-where-hush_planmd-breaks"&gt;Signal-by-Signal Audit (Where &lt;code&gt;HUSH_PLAN.md&lt;/code&gt; Breaks)&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;div class="table-wrapper-paragraph"&gt;&lt;table&gt;
&lt;thead&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;th&gt;Planned Mechanic in &lt;code&gt;HUSH_PLAN.md&lt;/code&gt;
&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;th&gt;Verdict&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;th&gt;Hard Technical Evidence&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;/thead&gt;
&lt;tbody&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Heartbeat waveform → live audio thump via peak detection&lt;/strong&gt; (&lt;code&gt;arterialPressureTrace&lt;/code&gt;)&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Unreliable / Brittle&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Per &lt;a href="https://presagetech.com/model-cards/arterial_pressure_model_card.html" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;Arterial Pressure Model Card&lt;/a&gt;, waveform Pearson &lt;em&gt;r&lt;/em&gt; is &lt;code&gt;0.68–0.74&lt;/code&gt; even in lab conditions, and high-confidence return rate drops from &lt;code&gt;93.2%&lt;/code&gt; (Fitzpatrick I) to &lt;strong&gt;&lt;code&gt;45.1%&lt;/code&gt; (Type VI)&lt;/strong&gt; (&lt;code&gt;40.4%&lt;/code&gt; lamp, &lt;code&gt;34.2%&lt;/code&gt; window). Micro-motion, facial expressions, and dark lighting cause false peaks. Furthermore, sample timestamps are already in the past due to pipeline latency—you cannot schedule them directly without latency offset, bandpass smoothing, refractory clamping, and &lt;code&gt;pulseRate&lt;/code&gt; fallback.&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Over-110 BPM triggers &lt;code&gt;"Your heart is pounding"&lt;/code&gt; invalid-reading event&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Contradicts Model Card + Low Trigger Odds&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Overview docs say &lt;code&gt;40–110 BPM&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;strong&gt;but&lt;/strong&gt; the actual &lt;code&gt;2026-11-06&lt;/code&gt; Arterial Pressure &amp;amp; HRV Model Cards state &lt;strong&gt;&lt;code&gt;40–180 BPM&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;. Seated adults playing a 2D canvas game also rarely sustain &amp;gt;110 BPM over a 10.6–12 s rolling average.&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Statue room: figures move while eyes are closed via &lt;code&gt;face.blinking&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Broken / Cheesable&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Multiple contestants (&lt;code&gt;Hear Me&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;Don't Blink&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;Breathless Reef&lt;/code&gt;) verified &lt;code&gt;face.blinking&lt;/code&gt; only emits a &lt;strong&gt;brief onset pulse (~130–180 ms, ~100–150 ms lag)&lt;/strong&gt;—it &lt;strong&gt;does not stay &lt;code&gt;true&lt;/code&gt; when you hold your eyes shut&lt;/strong&gt;. A player can literally close their eyes and walk straight through the statue room! You must compute &lt;strong&gt;Eye Aspect Ratio (EAR)&lt;/strong&gt; from &lt;code&gt;face.landmarks&lt;/code&gt; (plus handle landmark dropouts on tight blinks).&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Candle steadiness from &lt;code&gt;breathing.upperTrace&lt;/code&gt; + &lt;code&gt;breathing.rate&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;&lt;strong&gt;High Setup Friction + Conflict&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Breathing requires &lt;strong&gt;face + upper chest/shoulders visible&lt;/strong&gt; (tested at &lt;strong&gt;36 inches / 3 ft&lt;/strong&gt; on a tripod C920) and &lt;strong&gt;&lt;code&gt;30–45 s&lt;/code&gt; uninterrupted warm-up&lt;/strong&gt;; normal laptop distance routinely fires &lt;code&gt;CHEST_NOT_VISIBLE&lt;/code&gt; (&lt;code&gt;@nightshift-unlav&lt;/code&gt;'s &lt;em&gt;Hush&lt;/em&gt; calibration took &lt;strong&gt;&amp;gt;2 minutes&lt;/strong&gt; because of this). &lt;code&gt;breathing.rate&lt;/code&gt; is a sluggish 30 s average, &lt;code&gt;upperTrace&lt;/code&gt; stability drops when changing pace or talking, and trace polarity can invert depending on camera tilt.&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Screen pulsing + guttering candle in a dark-game aesthetic&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Self-Sabotage Feedback Loop&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Presage explicitly warns that &lt;strong&gt;low light&lt;/strong&gt; forces webcams to drop exposure FPS (causing fatal &lt;code&gt;kSustainedLowFrameRate&lt;/code&gt;) and &lt;strong&gt;flickering screen illumination on the face breaks PPG/pulse readings with deceptively high confidence&lt;/strong&gt;. A pulsing/guttering monitor in a dim room injects artificial flicker at your heartbeat/breath frequency right onto your face.&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Talking = monster "hears you instantly"&lt;/strong&gt; (&lt;code&gt;face.talking&lt;/code&gt;)&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;&lt;strong&gt;UX Mismatch&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;
&lt;code&gt;face.talking&lt;/code&gt; is &lt;strong&gt;visual lip-movement detection only&lt;/strong&gt; (no microphone). Silent yawns/sighs/jaw tension trigger false chases, while whispers or sharp audible gasps with closed lips go undetected.&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;&lt;strong&gt;60 s Parlour Calibration + HRV warm-up&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Bad UX / Dead Signal&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Per &lt;a href="https://presagetech.com/model-cards/hrv_model_card.html" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;HRV Model Card&lt;/a&gt;, HRV outputs &lt;strong&gt;1 sample per 60 s&lt;/strong&gt;, requires 60 s of continuous stillness, and drops to &lt;code&gt;42.0%&lt;/code&gt; return rate on Type VI (&lt;code&gt;6.3%&lt;/code&gt; under window light!). A 60 s motionless tutorial before gameplay starts will lose judges fast.&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Testing via recorded video (&lt;code&gt;useCustomInput()&lt;/code&gt; + &lt;code&gt;sendFrame()&lt;/code&gt;)&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Wrong SDK Pattern&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Presage's documented &lt;a href="https://smartspectra.presagetech.com/docs/nodejs/headless-testing-in-ci" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;Headless Testing in CI&lt;/a&gt; uses &lt;strong&gt;&lt;code&gt;sdk.useFile(videoPath)&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;, not raw frame decoding into &lt;code&gt;useCustomInput()&lt;/code&gt;.&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Bundler &amp;amp; Payload Handling&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Implementation Traps&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Renderer code must import strictly from &lt;code&gt;@smartspectra/node-sdk/renderer&lt;/code&gt; and &lt;code&gt;@smartspectra/node-sdk/messages&lt;/code&gt; (importing root &lt;code&gt;@smartspectra/node-sdk&lt;/code&gt; drags &lt;code&gt;koffi&lt;/code&gt; into the renderer bundle, and root &lt;code&gt;decodeMetrics&lt;/code&gt; returns a raw &lt;code&gt;Buffer&lt;/code&gt; unless &lt;code&gt;setMetricsClass&lt;/code&gt; is called). Also &lt;code&gt;metrics&lt;/code&gt; emits &lt;strong&gt;batched slices&lt;/strong&gt;—reading only &lt;code&gt;.at(-1)&lt;/code&gt; drops blink/talking events that occurred mid-batch.&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;/tbody&gt;
&lt;/table&gt;&lt;/div&gt;


&lt;h3 id="agent-session-1410-1--community-wisdom"&gt;🌐 Community Wisdom&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;👁️ &lt;a href="https://dev.to/zuhairhalawa/dont-blink-a-horror-game-where-your-blinks-let-it-closer-58ba"&gt;Don't Blink: a horror game where your blinks let it closer&lt;/a&gt; &lt;a href="https://dev.to/zuhairhalawa"&gt;@zuhairhalawa&lt;/a&gt; — Proved &lt;code&gt;face.blinking&lt;/code&gt; lasts 130–180 ms as a blink onset and fails to fire when eyes are held shut, requiring local landmark Eye Aspect Ratio tracking and a 30 fps canvas cap to stop 11-second CPU processing crashes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;👻 &lt;a href="https://dev.to/jenniferevangelistade/ghost-hunt-who-else-was-there-every-face-has-a-heartbeat-except-one-1jcg"&gt;Ghost Hunt · Who Else Was There? Every face has a heartbeat. Except one.&lt;/a&gt; &lt;a href="https://dev.to/jenniferevangelistade"&gt;@jenniferevangelistade&lt;/a&gt; — Found that SmartSpectra returns HTTP 403 in cloud CI runners and unsigned DLL blocks under Windows Smart App Control, so gating confidence (&lt;code&gt;&amp;gt;= 50%&lt;/code&gt;) and providing a tagged sample-data mode keeps judges unblocked.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;🫁 &lt;a href="https://dev.to/wst2002rk/hear-me-a-long-blink-becomes-a-voice-using-only-a-laptop-webcam-1jk7"&gt;Hear Me: a long blink becomes a voice, using only a laptop webcam&lt;/a&gt; &lt;a href="https://dev.to/wst2002rk"&gt;@wst2002rk&lt;/a&gt; — Observed that &lt;code&gt;1280×720&lt;/code&gt; capture starved a laptop CPU below SmartSpectra's 25 fps minimum while &lt;code&gt;640×360&lt;/code&gt; held 30 fps, and that virtual cameras listed first in &lt;code&gt;getUserMedia&lt;/code&gt; must be skipped explicitly.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;🏮 &lt;a href="https://dev.to/dhananjayachamod0754/kuudu-breathe-a-vesak-lantern-home-with-your-breath-2mph"&gt;Kuudu: Breathe a Vesak Lantern Home with Your Breath&lt;/a&gt; &lt;a href="https://dev.to/dhananjayachamod0754"&gt;@dhananjayachamod0754&lt;/a&gt; — Documented that &lt;code&gt;breathing.rate&lt;/code&gt; is too slow (~30 s trailing average) for real-time control and that waveform &lt;code&gt;stable&lt;/code&gt; drops whenever pace changes, requiring raw &lt;code&gt;breathing.upperTrace&lt;/code&gt; with drift removal and user-flippable polarity.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;👵 &lt;a href="https://dev.to/ansellmaximilian/granny-is-watching-a-reactive-horror-experience-using-smartpectra-54b7"&gt;Granny Is Watching: A Reactive Horror Experience Using SmartPectra&lt;/a&gt; &lt;a href="https://dev.to/ansellmaximilian"&gt;@ansellmaximilian&lt;/a&gt; — Highlighted that SmartSpectra's Nov 3, 2026 SDK Privacy Policy ties automatic Anthropic LLM Insights to active cardio+breathing sessions and leaves SDK-managed &lt;code&gt;%LOCALAPPDATA%\SmartSpectraSDK&lt;/code&gt; cache outside app deletion controls.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;


&lt;h2 id="agent-session-1410-1-summary--concrete-decision-before-you-write-line-1"&gt;Summary &amp;amp; Concrete Decision Before You Write Line 1&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;You have &lt;strong&gt;5.5 days&lt;/strong&gt; left and &lt;strong&gt;zero code written&lt;/strong&gt; yet. Keep the stack (&lt;code&gt;Electron&lt;/code&gt; + &lt;code&gt;@smartspectra/node-sdk@3.5.0&lt;/code&gt; at &lt;code&gt;640×480&lt;/code&gt;), fix the privacy disclosures, and make one strategic call &lt;strong&gt;today&lt;/strong&gt;:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ol&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;If you pivot concept (Recommended for winning):&lt;/strong&gt; Drop the crowded "monster hears your heartbeat / blink statues" trope completely—you cannot beat four already-shipped horror entries (including one literally called &lt;em&gt;Hush&lt;/em&gt;) on Originality in five days. Look for an uncrowded angle in &lt;em&gt;Most Creative or Delightful Use&lt;/em&gt; or &lt;em&gt;Best Thoughtful Real-World Use&lt;/em&gt; where &lt;strong&gt;facial landmarks + blink/EAR + expressions + pulse/breath&lt;/strong&gt; fit naturally &lt;em&gt;without&lt;/em&gt; requiring a dark room or 60-second stillness (for instance, a &lt;strong&gt;face/expression/pulse-driven Nigerian "NEPA / generator" narrative puzzle, negotiation/market-haggling game, or playful real-world focus/accessibility utility&lt;/strong&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;If you insist on keeping the horror compound game:&lt;/strong&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Rename it immediately&lt;/strong&gt; (do &lt;strong&gt;not&lt;/strong&gt; use "Hush").&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Drop the 60 s parlour, drop HRV, drop &lt;code&gt;&amp;gt;110 BPM&lt;/code&gt; gating, and drop raw &lt;code&gt;arterialPressureTrace&lt;/code&gt; peak-thumps&lt;/strong&gt; (drive thumps smoothly from &lt;code&gt;pulseRate&lt;/code&gt; or a visual/audio heartbeat once settled, and start gameplay within 12–15 s).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Fix blink detection&lt;/strong&gt; using &lt;code&gt;face.landmarks&lt;/code&gt; EAR so holding eyes shut advances statues rapidly instead of cheesing them.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Protect lighting:&lt;/strong&gt; Require a well-lit room, use dark muted colors &lt;em&gt;without&lt;/em&gt; rhythmic screen-brightness pulsing/flicker on the face, and calibrate &lt;code&gt;640×480&lt;/code&gt; capture first via a 15-minute &lt;code&gt;electron-quickstart&lt;/code&gt; run on your actual Windows webcam today.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Rewrite Section 4 consent copy honestly:&lt;/strong&gt; Either omit &lt;code&gt;cardioMetrics&lt;/code&gt; or &lt;code&gt;breathingMetrics&lt;/code&gt; if you want to truthfully avoid automatic Anthropic Insights—&lt;strong&gt;or&lt;/strong&gt; explicitly disclose Presage's automatic Insights (Anthropic), device/app attestation, IP/usage logging, and separate SDK cache, and remove the word "anonymous."&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
