&lt;p&gt;Here is the unvarnished audit: &lt;strong&gt;90% of "obvious" Presage pivot ideas are already crowded or physically broken on a Windows laptop.&lt;/strong&gt; Below are the traps you must avoid, the SDK physics that dictate what actually wins, and the &lt;strong&gt;3 genuinely original &lt;code&gt;0 / 101&lt;/code&gt; concepts&lt;/strong&gt; worth building.&lt;/p&gt;


&lt;h3 id="agent-session-1410-3-1-where-the-101-live-entries-actually-clustered-and-4-clever-trap-ideas-to-kill-immediately"&gt;1. Where the 101 Live Entries Actually Clustered (and 4 "Clever" Trap Ideas to Kill Immediately)&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Excluding ~19 spam/empty posts, ~82 real &lt;code&gt;#presagechallenge&lt;/code&gt; entries already occupy almost every predictable webcam-biometric category:&lt;br&gt;
- &lt;strong&gt;Breathing gardens, pets, pacers &amp;amp; check-ins (~24+):&lt;/strong&gt; &lt;em&gt;Exhale&lt;/em&gt; (&lt;code&gt;R=25&lt;/code&gt;), &lt;em&gt;Tiny Cat&lt;/em&gt; (&lt;code&gt;R=20&lt;/code&gt;), &lt;em&gt;Health Check-Up&lt;/em&gt; (&lt;code&gt;R=14&lt;/code&gt;), &lt;em&gt;Roll Call&lt;/em&gt; (&lt;code&gt;bin4yi&lt;/code&gt;), &lt;em&gt;Stillpoint&lt;/em&gt;, &lt;em&gt;Breathgarden&lt;/em&gt;, &lt;em&gt;VitalFlow&lt;/em&gt;, &lt;em&gt;PulseVerse&lt;/em&gt;, &lt;em&gt;Nidra&lt;/em&gt;.&lt;br&gt;
- &lt;strong&gt;Speaking, interview &amp;amp; recitation coaches (~9+):&lt;/strong&gt; &lt;em&gt;PitchPulse&lt;/em&gt; (&lt;code&gt;R=47&lt;/code&gt;), &lt;em&gt;Beyond the Words&lt;/em&gt; (stuttering), &lt;em&gt;Ma&lt;/em&gt; (&lt;code&gt;useFile&lt;/code&gt;-tested teleprompter), &lt;em&gt;HalfBeat&lt;/em&gt;, &lt;em&gt;Hot Seat&lt;/em&gt;, &lt;em&gt;Rehearse&lt;/em&gt;, &lt;em&gt;Saktah&lt;/em&gt; (Qur'an tajwid pauses), &lt;em&gt;StagePulse&lt;/em&gt;, &lt;em&gt;VTU viva&lt;/em&gt;.&lt;br&gt;
- &lt;strong&gt;Horror, lie-detector, diving &amp;amp; breathing games (~10):&lt;/strong&gt; &lt;em&gt;Granny Is Watching&lt;/em&gt; (&lt;code&gt;R=10&lt;/code&gt;), &lt;em&gt;Breathless Reef&lt;/em&gt; (&lt;code&gt;R=5&lt;/code&gt;), &lt;em&gt;CalmRR&lt;/em&gt;, &lt;em&gt;Poker Face&lt;/em&gt;, &lt;em&gt;Cool Vitals&lt;/em&gt;, &lt;em&gt;Body Radar&lt;/em&gt;, &lt;em&gt;Kuudu&lt;/em&gt;, &lt;em&gt;Hush&lt;/em&gt;, &lt;em&gt;Don't Blink&lt;/em&gt;, &lt;em&gt;Ghost Hunt&lt;/em&gt;.&lt;br&gt;
- &lt;strong&gt;Blink/gaze AAC &amp;amp; hands-free control (~5):&lt;/strong&gt; &lt;em&gt;Hear Me&lt;/em&gt; (&lt;code&gt;R=47&lt;/code&gt;), &lt;em&gt;Spatial Communicator&lt;/em&gt; (&lt;code&gt;R=12&lt;/code&gt;), &lt;em&gt;Glimra&lt;/em&gt; (head-turn PDFs), &lt;em&gt;OnBlink&lt;/em&gt;, &lt;em&gt;Kitchen Chaos&lt;/em&gt; (smile/head-tilt recipes), &lt;em&gt;Ultra Talking Pulse&lt;/em&gt;.&lt;br&gt;
- &lt;strong&gt;Developer/AI gates &amp;amp; focus (~6+):&lt;/strong&gt; &lt;em&gt;ZenDev&lt;/em&gt;, &lt;em&gt;Proof of Breath&lt;/em&gt; (&lt;code&gt;DROP TABLE&lt;/code&gt; breath gate), &lt;em&gt;Rubber Duck Gate&lt;/em&gt;, &lt;em&gt;Commit Pulse&lt;/em&gt;, &lt;em&gt;Zwischenzug&lt;/em&gt; (chess tilt lock), &lt;em&gt;CodeCalm&lt;/em&gt;, &lt;em&gt;CalmDesk AI&lt;/em&gt;.&lt;br&gt;
- &lt;strong&gt;Generative art, audio &amp;amp; media testing (~7):&lt;/strong&gt; &lt;em&gt;Ad Pulse Lab&lt;/em&gt; (&lt;code&gt;R=21&lt;/code&gt;), &lt;em&gt;Glassbreath&lt;/em&gt; (&lt;code&gt;R=9&lt;/code&gt;), &lt;em&gt;Counterfeed&lt;/em&gt; (&lt;code&gt;R=6&lt;/code&gt;), &lt;em&gt;Retro Techno&lt;/em&gt; (&lt;code&gt;R=5&lt;/code&gt;), &lt;em&gt;Second Guess&lt;/em&gt; (flashcard hesitation), &lt;em&gt;Breath Actor&lt;/em&gt;, &lt;em&gt;Breathblown&lt;/em&gt;, &lt;em&gt;Tidal Loom&lt;/em&gt;, &lt;em&gt;PulseTones&lt;/em&gt;, &lt;em&gt;Pulse Postcards&lt;/em&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Before looking at winners, kill these &lt;strong&gt;4 tempting ideas that look original on paper but fail engineering reality&lt;/strong&gt;:&lt;br&gt;
1. &lt;strong&gt;rPPG Deepfake / AI-Avatar Video Detector (&lt;code&gt;useFile&lt;/code&gt;):&lt;/strong&gt; H.264 video compression destroys the tiny optical PPG color shift even on real humans (&lt;em&gt;HalfBeat&lt;/em&gt; empirically saw a real Pexels talking head spike &lt;code&gt;55 -&amp;gt; 73 -&amp;gt; 91 bpm&lt;/code&gt; in 3 seconds), and Presage's Model Card (&lt;code&gt;arterial_pressure&lt;/code&gt;) shows &lt;code&gt;cardio.pulseRate&lt;/code&gt; return rate (&lt;code&gt;conf &amp;gt;= 97&lt;/code&gt;) drops from &lt;code&gt;93.2%&lt;/code&gt; (Fitzpatrick I) to &lt;strong&gt;&lt;code&gt;45.1%&lt;/code&gt; (Fitzpatrick VI)&lt;/strong&gt;, &lt;code&gt;40.4%&lt;/code&gt; under indoor lamps, and &lt;code&gt;34.2%&lt;/code&gt; near windows. False-flagging real Black speakers as "no pulse / bot" would be a scientific disaster.&lt;br&gt;
2. &lt;strong&gt;Post-Workout Gym / HIIT Set-Recovery Timer:&lt;/strong&gt; &lt;code&gt;docs&lt;/code&gt; + Model Card lock valid &lt;code&gt;cardio.pulseRate&lt;/code&gt; to &lt;strong&gt;&lt;code&gt;40–110 BPM&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/strong&gt; and stationary subjects. Real post-set heart rate (&lt;code&gt;120–175 BPM&lt;/code&gt;), heavy panting, and sweat flush fall outside validated bounds.&lt;br&gt;
3. &lt;strong&gt;Late-Night Driver / Micro-Sleep Alert (&lt;code&gt;PERCLOS&lt;/code&gt;):&lt;/strong&gt; Nighttime dim cabins, headlight glare, and vehicle vibration violate stationary + even lighting requirements, and OpenCV PERCLOS detectors are a well-worn cliché.&lt;br&gt;
4. &lt;strong&gt;Windows Switch-Access Macro Keyboard (&lt;code&gt;koffi SendInput&lt;/code&gt;) or Local Voice-AI Turn-Taker:&lt;/strong&gt; Even though &lt;code&gt;koffi&lt;/code&gt; is bundled in &lt;code&gt;@smartspectra/node-sdk&lt;/code&gt;, keystroke macros only use landmarks (giving Presage zero reason to exist alongside &lt;em&gt;Hear Me&lt;/em&gt; at &lt;code&gt;R=47&lt;/code&gt;), and an 800 ms Voice-AI barge-in bot suffers both from the ~1 s &lt;code&gt;breathing.upperTrace&lt;/code&gt; pipeline lag and slow CPU inference if you have no local GPU.&lt;/p&gt;


&lt;h3 id="agent-session-1410-3-2-sdk--windows-physics-reality-verified-constraints"&gt;2. SDK &amp;amp; Windows Physics Reality (Verified Constraints)&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Design strictly around SmartSpectra's &lt;strong&gt;three true time horizons&lt;/strong&gt; on Windows:&lt;br&gt;
- &lt;strong&gt;Fast (&lt;code&gt;~30–60 ms&lt;/code&gt;):&lt;/strong&gt; &lt;code&gt;face.landmarks&lt;/code&gt; (478 2D &lt;code&gt;Point2dFloat&lt;/code&gt; points incl. iris centers &lt;code&gt;468–477&lt;/code&gt;), &lt;code&gt;face.blinking&lt;/code&gt; (&lt;code&gt;130–180 ms&lt;/code&gt; onset pulses — compute EAR from landmarks if you want held eye closure), &lt;code&gt;face.talking&lt;/code&gt; (silent visual lip speech), &lt;code&gt;face.expression&lt;/code&gt; (8 classes: &lt;code&gt;angry&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;contempt&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;disgust&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;fear&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;happy&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;sad&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;surprise&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;neutral&lt;/code&gt;).&lt;br&gt;
- &lt;strong&gt;Mid (&lt;code&gt;~1.0 s&lt;/code&gt; phase lag, &lt;code&gt;~20–30 Hz&lt;/code&gt; waveform):&lt;/strong&gt; &lt;code&gt;breathing.upperTrace&lt;/code&gt; (upper-chest wave — &lt;em&gt;Breath Actor&lt;/em&gt; verified ~1 s pipeline lag; also &lt;code&gt;generated.d.ts&lt;/code&gt; confirms &lt;code&gt;upperTrace&lt;/code&gt; inherits its &lt;code&gt;stable&lt;/code&gt; flag from &lt;code&gt;breathing.rate&lt;/code&gt;, so waiting on &lt;code&gt;upperTrace.stable === true&lt;/code&gt; stalls for 30+ seconds even when the waveform already tracks!). Crucially, per &lt;code&gt;mc_breathing.txt&lt;/code&gt;, breathing has &lt;strong&gt;77.9%–85.0% return rate across Fitzpatrick IV–VI&lt;/strong&gt; (&lt;code&gt;0.29–0.59 BrPM&lt;/code&gt; MAE), making chest breath far more inclusive on your own webcam and judges' diverse setups than pulse/HRV (&lt;code&gt;42%&lt;/code&gt; Type VI HRV return).&lt;br&gt;
- &lt;strong&gt;Slow (&lt;code&gt;12–60 s&lt;/code&gt;):&lt;/strong&gt; &lt;code&gt;breathing.rate&lt;/code&gt; (30 s window), &lt;code&gt;cardio.pulseRate&lt;/code&gt; (12 s window), &lt;code&gt;cardio.hrv&lt;/code&gt; (60 s window).&lt;br&gt;
- &lt;strong&gt;Hidden SDK &amp;amp; Policy Landmines:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;
  - &lt;code&gt;EDL&lt;/code&gt;/&lt;code&gt;GLUTES_MICROMOTION&lt;/code&gt;/&lt;code&gt;KNEES_MICROMOTION&lt;/code&gt; had &lt;strong&gt;0 working demos&lt;/strong&gt; in all 101 entries (&lt;code&gt;ffi.js&lt;/code&gt; warns &lt;code&gt;EDA_TRACE&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;ARTERIAL_PRESSURE_TRACE&lt;/code&gt;, and micromotion require encrypted device-key model loading via &lt;code&gt;Preconfigure&lt;/code&gt;); never gamble your core loop on &lt;code&gt;EDA&lt;/code&gt; or &lt;code&gt;micromotion&lt;/code&gt; without a Day-1 verification pass.&lt;br&gt;
  - Keep renderer/camera capture at &lt;code&gt;960×540&lt;/code&gt; (or capture natively in Node main via &lt;code&gt;CameraSelection.byId&lt;/code&gt;/&lt;code&gt;default&lt;/code&gt; — note &lt;code&gt;.front&lt;/code&gt;/&lt;code&gt;.back&lt;/code&gt; throw &lt;code&gt;kInputUnavailable&lt;/code&gt; on Windows!) to avoid &lt;code&gt;kSustainedLowFrameRate (14)&lt;/code&gt;.&lt;br&gt;
  - &lt;strong&gt;Privacy Policy §7.4 (Nov 3, 2026):&lt;/strong&gt; Enabling &lt;em&gt;both&lt;/em&gt; breathing and cardio triggers Presage's non-disableable Anthropic LLM Insights pipeline. &lt;strong&gt;Defaulting to &lt;code&gt;faceMetrics + breathingMetrics&lt;/code&gt; (without cardio)&lt;/strong&gt; avoids sending vitals to Anthropic unless the user explicitly enables optional cardio!&lt;/p&gt;


&lt;h3 id="agent-session-1410-3-3-three-original-0--101-pivot-angles-built-to-win"&gt;3. Three Original &lt;code&gt;0 / 101&lt;/code&gt; Pivot Angles Built to Win&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;p&gt;All three verified &lt;strong&gt;&lt;code&gt;0 hits&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/strong&gt; across all 101 titles/descriptions and 40+ inspected full bodies for their core outputs (&lt;code&gt;edl&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;murch&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;davinci&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;premiere&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;ffmpeg&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;jump cut&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;subtitle&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;Before Your Eyes&lt;/code&gt;-style non-horror vignette).&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h4 id="agent-session-1410-3-option-1-top-pick--best-thoughtful-real-world-use--overall"&gt;Option 1 (Top Pick — &lt;em&gt;Best Thoughtful Real-World Use&lt;/em&gt; / &lt;em&gt;Overall&lt;/em&gt;):&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;h3 id="agent-session-1410-3-murch-blinkcut--physiological-film--self-tape-cut-workbench-usefile--live-multi-take-cam"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;code&gt;MURCH&lt;/code&gt; (&lt;code&gt;BLINKCUT&lt;/code&gt;) — Physiological Film &amp;amp; Self-Tape Cut Workbench (&lt;code&gt;useFile()&lt;/code&gt; + Live Multi-Take Cam)&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;The Hook:&lt;/strong&gt; Audio-silence cutters like Descript/Premiere slice strictly by volume, chopping right through the speaker's &lt;strong&gt;pre-sentence inhale&lt;/strong&gt; (producing suffocating, robotic jump-cuts) and slicing mid-blink. In &lt;em&gt;In the Blink of an Eye&lt;/em&gt;, editor Walter Murch explained why real cinema cuts land on &lt;strong&gt;blinks&lt;/strong&gt; (mental punctuation) and &lt;strong&gt;completed exhales&lt;/strong&gt;.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Why Presage Is 100% Load-Bearing (and 1s Lag Disappears):&lt;/strong&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Runs &lt;strong&gt;&lt;code&gt;sdk.useFile(mp4Path, { interframeDelayMs: ... })&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/strong&gt; offline on stationary talking-head video, actor self-tapes, interview A-cam, or live multi-take webcam clips (&lt;code&gt;960×540&lt;/code&gt;). Because extraction runs over a recorded timeline, you time-align SmartSpectra's ~1 s &lt;code&gt;breathing.upperTrace&lt;/code&gt; phase offset and blink timestamps cleanly back to exact frames!&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Fuses &lt;strong&gt;&lt;code&gt;face.blinking&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/strong&gt; (clean cognitive cut points vs rapid stress flutter), &lt;strong&gt;&lt;code&gt;face.talking&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/strong&gt; (visual speech boundaries even on noisy or muted scratch audio), &lt;strong&gt;&lt;code&gt;breathing.upperTrace&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/strong&gt; (protects the &lt;strong&gt;0.5–1.0 s pre-speech inhale lead-in&lt;/strong&gt; so cuts never clip the breath-in, and cuts out at &lt;strong&gt;exhale troughs&lt;/strong&gt;), and &lt;strong&gt;&lt;code&gt;face.expression&lt;/code&gt; + &lt;code&gt;landmarks&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/strong&gt; (expression peaks &amp;amp; gaze stability for comparing Take 1 vs Take 2 vs Take 3).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;em&gt;Signal-honest degradation:&lt;/em&gt; If a tight head crop hides the chest (&lt;code&gt;upperTrace&lt;/code&gt; sparse), it visibly badges &lt;code&gt;"Head-only framing: Blink + Visual Speech cuts active (Breath lead-in unavailable)"&lt;/code&gt; instead of guessing. Defaults to &lt;code&gt;faceMetrics + breathingMetrics&lt;/code&gt; (zero Anthropic cardio telemetry unless user opts into Take-level pulse comparison).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Why Judges Love It in 15 Seconds:&lt;/strong&gt;

&lt;ol&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Live In-App A/B Cut Player:&lt;/strong&gt; Play the exact same messy 60 s raw take two ways back-to-back — &lt;strong&gt;Audio-Silence Cut&lt;/strong&gt; (clipped inhales, jarring mid-blink cuts) vs &lt;strong&gt;Blink+Exhale Cut&lt;/strong&gt; (natural cinema rhythm).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Real Industry Exports:&lt;/strong&gt; Valid &lt;strong&gt;CMX 3600 &lt;code&gt;.edl&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/strong&gt; (imports straight into DaVinci Resolve / Premiere Pro), frame marker &lt;code&gt;.csv&lt;/code&gt;, and an &lt;strong&gt;FFmpeg rough-cut &lt;code&gt;.mp4&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;!&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Meta Demo Hook:&lt;/strong&gt; Edit your &lt;em&gt;own&lt;/em&gt; hackathon submission intro using &lt;code&gt;MURCH&lt;/code&gt; on 3 live takes recorded in-app!&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ol&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Lethal Day-1 Spike to Run First:&lt;/strong&gt; Test &lt;code&gt;sdk.useFile(clip.mp4, { interframeDelayMs: 0 })&lt;/code&gt; vs &lt;code&gt;33&lt;/code&gt; on Windows H.264 &lt;code&gt;.mp4&lt;/code&gt; right now — measure wall-clock decode speed, confirm &lt;code&gt;kSustainedLowFrameRate&lt;/code&gt; never fires, and calibrate the exact &lt;code&gt;upperTrace&lt;/code&gt; frame lag against a clap/deep-inhale test clip.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;


&lt;h4 id="agent-session-1410-3-option-2-best-most-creative-or-delightful-use-alternate--live-webcam"&gt;Option 2 (&lt;em&gt;Best &lt;code&gt;Most Creative or Delightful Use&lt;/code&gt; Alternate — Live Webcam&lt;/em&gt;):&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;h3 id="agent-session-1410-3-afterimage--non-horror-interactive-memory-essay-driven-by-gaze-blinks--calm-breath"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;code&gt;AFTERIMAGE&lt;/code&gt; — Non-Horror Interactive Memory Essay Driven by Gaze, Blinks &amp;amp; Calm Breath&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;The Hook:&lt;/strong&gt; Inspired by BAFTA winner &lt;em&gt;Before Your Eyes&lt;/em&gt; — &lt;strong&gt;zero horror monsters, zero scare gauges (&lt;code&gt;CalmRR&lt;/code&gt;/&lt;code&gt;Granny&lt;/code&gt;/&lt;code&gt;Don't Blink&lt;/code&gt;), zero &lt;code&gt;Ghost Visitors&lt;/code&gt; personas, and zero "breathe slowly to inflate a cat/vase/lantern"&lt;/strong&gt;. You experience a 3-minute atmospheric typographic/procedural WebGL-canvas vignette where &lt;strong&gt;each natural blink cuts time forward&lt;/strong&gt;, &lt;strong&gt;coarse gaze shifts move attention across a scene (&lt;code&gt;landmarks&lt;/code&gt; L/Center/R — no 14 px fake accuracy)&lt;/strong&gt;, and &lt;strong&gt;rolling 4-second chest-breath regularity (&lt;code&gt;breathing.upperTrace&lt;/code&gt; low variance, immune to 1 s phase lag!) + calm facial softness&lt;/strong&gt; slows the scene drift so you linger inside hidden visual/audio memory layers before your next blink turns the page.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Why Presage Is Load-Bearing &amp;amp; Hardware-Safe:&lt;/strong&gt; Uses &lt;code&gt;&amp;lt;60 ms&lt;/code&gt; &lt;code&gt;face.blinking&lt;/code&gt; + coarse &lt;code&gt;landmarks&lt;/code&gt; gaze/brow + &lt;code&gt;face.expression&lt;/code&gt; (&lt;code&gt;sad&lt;/code&gt;/&lt;code&gt;happy&lt;/code&gt;/&lt;code&gt;neutral&lt;/code&gt;) for crisp interactions, paired with lag-tolerant rolling chest amplitude/variance (&lt;code&gt;breathing.upperTrace&lt;/code&gt;) + &lt;code&gt;breathing.rate&lt;/code&gt; (valid across Fitzpatrick I–VI). Zero cardio dependency, zero GPU/3D asset pipeline (built in crisp procedural Canvas/SVG + WebAudio), zero external API keys.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Brutal Weakness vs Option 1:&lt;/strong&gt; Interactive narrative essays live or die on writing, pacing, and sound craft in 5 days — if the prose/audio feels flat or forced, it looks smaller than a real tool like &lt;code&gt;MURCH&lt;/code&gt;. Only pick this if building an emotional art-piece excites you way more than video editing.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;


&lt;h4 id="agent-session-1410-3-option-3-best-accessibility-alternate-via-usefile"&gt;Option 3 (&lt;em&gt;Best Accessibility Alternate via &lt;code&gt;useFile()&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/em&gt;):&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;h3 id="agent-session-1410-3-subtext--non-verbal-subtext--breath-pause-vtt-annotator-for-unedited-interviews--self-study-videos"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;code&gt;SUBTEXT&lt;/code&gt; — Non-Verbal Subtext &amp;amp; Breath-Pause &lt;code&gt;.vtt&lt;/code&gt; Annotator for Unedited Interviews &amp;amp; Self-Study Videos&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;The Hook:&lt;/strong&gt; Auto-captions (&lt;code&gt;Whisper&lt;/code&gt;, YouTube CC) flatten human communication to bare words — erasing whether a speaker &lt;strong&gt;held their breath for 3.5 seconds before answering&lt;/strong&gt;, &lt;strong&gt;burst-blinked&lt;/strong&gt;, &lt;strong&gt;glanced off-axis while thinking&lt;/strong&gt;, or &lt;strong&gt;forced a tight smile (&lt;code&gt;expression&lt;/code&gt; + jaw landmarks)&lt;/strong&gt; on muted or spoken video. Drop any talking-head lecture/interview &lt;code&gt;.mp4&lt;/code&gt; (&lt;code&gt;useFile()&lt;/code&gt;) + optional &lt;code&gt;.srt&lt;/code&gt;/transcript -&amp;gt; outputs a rich &lt;strong&gt;Subtext &lt;code&gt;.vtt&lt;/code&gt; + interactive split viewer&lt;/strong&gt; tagging verified physical cues alongside words (&lt;code&gt;[inhale pause · 1.2s]&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;[eyes averted during pause]&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;[smile fade]&lt;/code&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Brutal Weakness vs Option 1:&lt;/strong&gt; &lt;strong&gt;Do not sugarcoat this:&lt;/strong&gt; without Deaf/Hard-of-Hearing co-testers in 5 days, inventing caption cue conventions risks feeling presumptuous or visually cluttered compared to &lt;strong&gt;&lt;code&gt;MURCH&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;, where any human judge immediately &lt;em&gt;hears and feels&lt;/em&gt; an A/B video cut improvement AND can open the exported &lt;code&gt;.edl&lt;/code&gt; in DaVinci Resolve. (&lt;code&gt;MURCH&lt;/code&gt; is strictly stronger on both proof and universal delight.)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;


