&lt;h3 id="agent-session-1410-5-1-honest-review-of-afterimage-as-of-nov-19-88-hours-left"&gt;1. Honest Review of &lt;strong&gt;AFTERIMAGE&lt;/strong&gt; (as of Nov 19, ~88 Hours Left)&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;p&gt;A fresh scrape of DEV (&lt;code&gt;#presagechallenge&lt;/code&gt;) right now shows &lt;strong&gt;105 entries&lt;/strong&gt; (&lt;code&gt;17&lt;/code&gt; published since Nov 17), including &lt;em&gt;STEADY&lt;/em&gt; (breath-aimed rifle crosshair), &lt;em&gt;CrossRoads&lt;/em&gt; (&lt;code&gt;R=24&lt;/code&gt;, imagining two life choices while monitoring pulse), &lt;em&gt;Idlewild&lt;/em&gt; (breath animation), &lt;em&gt;TrustFall&lt;/em&gt; (replaying a recorded minute to crash-test the SDK's &lt;code&gt;stable&lt;/code&gt; flag), and &lt;em&gt;Feltbeat&lt;/em&gt; (counting heartbeats without looking). Top reaction leaders are &lt;em&gt;PitchPulse&lt;/em&gt; (&lt;code&gt;R=54&lt;/code&gt;) and &lt;em&gt;Hear Me&lt;/em&gt; (&lt;code&gt;R=53&lt;/code&gt;).&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Overlap with AFTERIMAGE: &lt;code&gt;0 / 105&lt;/code&gt;.&lt;/strong&gt; No entry builds a non-horror interactive memory essay around &lt;strong&gt;blinks-as-cuts + coarse gaze focus + rolling breath clarity + an exportable Contact Sheet&lt;/strong&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Where &lt;strong&gt;AFTERIMAGE&lt;/strong&gt; can win &lt;em&gt;Most Creative or Delightful Use&lt;/em&gt; (or &lt;em&gt;Overall&lt;/em&gt;) — and where it can still fail:&lt;br&gt;
- &lt;strong&gt;Why it beats a &lt;em&gt;Before Your Eyes&lt;/em&gt; clone:&lt;/strong&gt; Blinks cut forward (&lt;code&gt;~30–60 ms&lt;/code&gt; via &lt;code&gt;face.blinking&lt;/code&gt; + EAR from &lt;code&gt;landmarks&lt;/code&gt;), coarse 3-zone gaze (&lt;code&gt;L / C / R&lt;/code&gt; from iris landmarks — never pretending pixel-line eye-tracking at &lt;code&gt;960×540&lt;/code&gt;) shifts parallax focus, and &lt;strong&gt;rolling 4 s chest-breath steadiness&lt;/strong&gt; (&lt;code&gt;breathing.upperTrace&lt;/code&gt;) acts like darkroom fixative that slows scene drift and develops hidden marginalia. Because steadiness is variance over 4 seconds, it stays immune to SmartSpectra's ~1 s &lt;code&gt;upperTrace&lt;/code&gt; pipeline lag.&lt;br&gt;
- &lt;strong&gt;Why skipping &lt;code&gt;cardioMetrics&lt;/code&gt; by default is a deliberate edge:&lt;/strong&gt; &lt;code&gt;mc_breathing&lt;/code&gt; is far more consistent across darker skin tones and laptop lamps than pulse/HRV, and omitting cardio means Presage's Nov 3 §7.4 automatic Anthropic LLM Insights payload is &lt;strong&gt;not triggered&lt;/strong&gt; — strengthening your &lt;em&gt;Consent &amp;amp; Data Handling&lt;/em&gt; section.&lt;br&gt;
- &lt;strong&gt;Architecture edge:&lt;/strong&gt; Capture runs in Node main at &lt;code&gt;960×540 @ 30fps&lt;/code&gt; using &lt;code&gt;CameraSelection.default&lt;/code&gt; / &lt;code&gt;.byId()&lt;/code&gt; (avoiding Windows &lt;code&gt;.front&lt;/code&gt;/&lt;code&gt;.back&lt;/code&gt; &lt;code&gt;kInputUnavailable&lt;/code&gt; crashes and Electron IPC &lt;code&gt;kSustainedLowFrameRate&lt;/code&gt; stalls). Only 478 wireframe coordinates and breath scalars go over WebSocket to the UI — zero raw camera video touches the browser.&lt;br&gt;
- &lt;strong&gt;Honest risks to manage ruthlessly before Mon Nov 23, 8:59 AM WAT:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;
  1. &lt;strong&gt;Writing &amp;amp; procedural atmosphere in ~88 hours:&lt;/strong&gt; Weak prose or flat visuals kill a narrative piece fast. Keep scope locked to &lt;strong&gt;5 tight procedural scenes (~3–4 min total)&lt;/strong&gt; plus procedural WebAudio ambience — no illustrated sprite assets or voice acting.&lt;br&gt;
  2. &lt;strong&gt;Avoid "wellness" cliché creep:&lt;/strong&gt; Make holding a steady breath feel like &lt;em&gt;photographic exposure clearing grain on an old memory&lt;/em&gt;, never a meditation guide scolding you to "breathe at 6 BrPM."&lt;br&gt;
  3. &lt;strong&gt;Live webcam proof before UI:&lt;/strong&gt; We still haven't measured your real &lt;code&gt;Integrated Camera&lt;/code&gt; FPS, coordinate units (&lt;code&gt;0..1&lt;/code&gt; vs px), or &lt;code&gt;upperTrace&lt;/code&gt; stability with a real key yet (&lt;code&gt;npm run spike&lt;/code&gt; resolves all three in 20 seconds).&lt;/p&gt;


