&lt;p&gt;Here is the exact, line-cited forensic breakdown—zero sugarcoating.&lt;/p&gt;


&lt;h3 id="agent-session-1410-9-1-what-is-broken-fake-or-half-baked-right-now"&gt;1. What Is Broken, Fake, or Half-Baked Right Now&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;h4 id="agent-session-1410-9-critical-live-camera--react-bugs"&gt;Critical Live-Camera &amp;amp; React Bugs&lt;/h4&gt;

&lt;ol&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Blink pacing is broken for real humans&lt;/strong&gt; (&lt;code&gt;signal-processor.mjs&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;ExperiencePage.tsx&lt;/code&gt;):

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Humans blink naturally every ~3–4 seconds. Right now &lt;strong&gt;every blink after 320 ms immediately cuts to the next beat&lt;/strong&gt;, meaning a normal viewer blasts through all 15 beats in ~45 seconds before they can read two sentences or let the 4.5 s breath window settle.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Worse: in &lt;code&gt;signal-processor.mjs&lt;/code&gt; L163–174, &lt;code&gt;blinkCut&lt;/code&gt; fires the millisecond eyelids &lt;strong&gt;close&lt;/strong&gt;, so trying to hold a &lt;code&gt;1.1 s&lt;/code&gt; long blink to &lt;strong&gt;pause&lt;/strong&gt; accidentally cuts forward first. Blink cuts must fire on &lt;strong&gt;eye reopen&lt;/strong&gt; (when closure &lt;code&gt;&amp;lt; 650 ms&lt;/code&gt;), gated by a visible &lt;strong&gt;"shutter armed" dwell period&lt;/strong&gt; (~4.5 s per beat, like &lt;em&gt;Before Your Eyes&lt;/em&gt;' metronome cue).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;&lt;code&gt;ExperiencePage&lt;/code&gt; fires a state-update loop on every signal packet (~30×/sec)&lt;/strong&gt; (&lt;code&gt;ExperiencePage.tsx&lt;/code&gt; &amp;amp; &lt;code&gt;L122-L127&lt;/code&gt;):

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;code&gt;flushSceneStats&lt;/code&gt; depends on &lt;code&gt;signal.breathSteadiness&lt;/code&gt; and &lt;code&gt;signal.breathWave&lt;/code&gt;, and &lt;code&gt;useEffect(..., [flushSceneStats, sceneIdx])&lt;/code&gt; invokes it in cleanup—meaning &lt;strong&gt;every incoming SmartSpectra frame triggers &lt;code&gt;commitSceneStats&lt;/code&gt; → &lt;code&gt;setReport&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;, re-rendering the entire &lt;code&gt;SessionProvider&lt;/code&gt; tree 25–30 times/sec.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;&lt;code&gt;Shift&lt;/code&gt; steady-breath shortcut breaks immediately&lt;/strong&gt; (&lt;code&gt;ExperiencePage.tsx&lt;/code&gt;):

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The &lt;code&gt;keydown&lt;/code&gt; effect depends on &lt;code&gt;signal.breathSteadiness&lt;/code&gt;, so holding &lt;code&gt;Shift&lt;/code&gt; increments once, re-runs the effect cleanup, and clears &lt;code&gt;shiftInterval&lt;/code&gt; after 120 ms.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Camera stop/start race condition on &lt;code&gt;Enter Scene I&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/strong&gt; (&lt;code&gt;CalibratePage.tsx&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;SessionContext.tsx&lt;/code&gt;):

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Clicking &lt;code&gt;Enter Scene I →&lt;/code&gt; calls &lt;code&gt;eraseSession()&lt;/code&gt; (which sends &lt;code&gt;{ type: 'stop' }&lt;/code&gt;) and 1 ms later sends &lt;code&gt;{ type: 'start' }&lt;/code&gt;. On the bridge, async &lt;code&gt;stopAsync()+destroy()&lt;/code&gt; races with &lt;code&gt;startCapture()&lt;/code&gt;, AND if the user already tested/warmed up the camera on &lt;code&gt;/calibrate&lt;/code&gt;, entering Scene I kills the stream and resets their breathing buffer to cold start.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Also &lt;code&gt;useSignals.ts&lt;/code&gt; L51 hardcodes initial &lt;code&gt;source = 'keyboard'&lt;/code&gt; even when &lt;code&gt;http://&lt;span class="agent-session-redacted"&gt;[REDACTED]&lt;/span&gt;:4199/health&lt;/code&gt; responds &lt;code&gt;ok&lt;/code&gt;.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Unverified &lt;code&gt;960×540&lt;/code&gt; aspect-ratio EAR threshold &amp;amp; zero real seated webcam data yet&lt;/strong&gt; (&lt;code&gt;signal-processor.mjs&lt;/code&gt;):

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Because the earlier background spike saw &lt;code&gt;kNoFaceFound&lt;/code&gt;, we still haven't empirically observed whether Windows SmartSpectra &lt;code&gt;face.landmarks&lt;/code&gt; returns &lt;code&gt;[0..1]&lt;/code&gt; normalized coords or &lt;code&gt;[0..960, 0..540]&lt;/code&gt; pixels. If &lt;code&gt;[0..1]&lt;/code&gt; on a &lt;code&gt;16:9&lt;/code&gt; frame, vertical &lt;code&gt;dy&lt;/code&gt; is stretched by &lt;code&gt;1.78×&lt;/code&gt; relative to &lt;code&gt;dx&lt;/code&gt; (our unit test at &lt;code&gt;signal-processor.test.mjs&lt;/code&gt; L51 only tested &lt;code&gt;960×960&lt;/code&gt; uniform scale!), which would inflate EAR and stop EAR-fallback blinks from triggering below &lt;code&gt;0.19&lt;/code&gt;.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Also missing: a &lt;code&gt;face.talking&lt;/code&gt; guard (speaking invalidates chest breathing per Presage's Model Card).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ol&gt;
&lt;h4 id="agent-session-1410-9-half-baked--placeholder-features"&gt;Half-Baked / Placeholder Features&lt;/h4&gt;

&lt;ol&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;PNG Contact Sheet export throws away all 5 scene artworks&lt;/strong&gt; (&lt;code&gt;exportSheet.ts&lt;/code&gt;):

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;On screen, &lt;code&gt;/contact-sheet&lt;/code&gt; shows 5 distinct miniature illustrations (&lt;code&gt;PlateThumb&lt;/code&gt;). When you click &lt;strong&gt;Download Print (.png)&lt;/strong&gt;, &lt;code&gt;exportSheet.ts&lt;/code&gt; ignores them and draws &lt;strong&gt;5 identical empty circles (&lt;code&gt;ctx.arc(..., 38)&lt;/code&gt;)&lt;/strong&gt;.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;The "Recorded Sample Trace" is fake&lt;/strong&gt; (&lt;code&gt;sample-trace.json&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;server.mjs&lt;/code&gt;):

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;code&gt;sample-trace.json&lt;/code&gt; is 24 hand-typed synthetic lines, and &lt;code&gt;record_export&lt;/code&gt; in &lt;code&gt;bridge/server.mjs&lt;/code&gt; is just an empty &lt;code&gt;ack&lt;/code&gt; stub—not a real SmartSpectra session recorder.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;The scenes don't actually *breathe&lt;/strong&gt;* (&lt;code&gt;SceneArt.tsx&lt;/code&gt;):

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Right now &lt;code&gt;SceneArt&lt;/code&gt; is clean flat architectural vector art where breath only changes an SVG Gaussian blur (&lt;code&gt;feGaussianBlur&lt;/code&gt;) and gaze jumps a hard rectangular opacity mask. Your real-time chest wave (&lt;code&gt;upperTrace&lt;/code&gt;) never organically moves steam, rain, lamp glow, or floating dust—and &lt;code&gt;ContactSheetPage.tsx&lt;/code&gt; L117–120 draws fabricated sine waves for unvisited scenes instead of honestly marking them empty.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Soundscape is minimal:&lt;/strong&gt; &lt;code&gt;soundscape.ts&lt;/code&gt; plays 3 bare sine/triangle oscillators—no soft rain/room ambience or subtle harmonic bloom when marginalia develops.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ol&gt;


&lt;h3 id="agent-session-1410-9-2-deep-competitive-audit-can-current-afterimage-beat-the-top-most-creative-or-delightful-use-rivals"&gt;2. Deep Competitive Audit: Can Current &lt;code&gt;AFTERIMAGE&lt;/code&gt; Beat the Top &lt;em&gt;Most Creative or Delightful Use&lt;/em&gt; Rivals?&lt;/h3&gt;

