&lt;p&gt;The &lt;strong&gt;engineering and live hardware telemetry&lt;/strong&gt; behind &lt;strong&gt;AFTERIMAGE&lt;/strong&gt; are genuinely strong enough to win. In fact, after reading the top competing &lt;code&gt;#presagechallenge&lt;/code&gt; entries just now, you solved problems that several top contenders openly admitted they couldn't solve.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;However, the current write-up is written in the voice of your non-winning Week 1 &amp;amp; Week 2 posts (&lt;em&gt;StrollerPulse&lt;/em&gt; and &lt;em&gt;SlipsLedger&lt;/em&gt;)—not in the voice of your Week 4 winner (&lt;em&gt;Ghost Visitors&lt;/em&gt;) or &lt;em&gt;Òjà&lt;/em&gt;.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Since DEV recently replaced volunteer community judging with &lt;strong&gt;MLH Coaches&lt;/strong&gt; (&lt;a href="https://dev.to/devteam/an-update-on-how-we-judge-dev-challenges-34eg"&gt;An Update on How We Judge DEV Challenges&lt;/a&gt;), your post is being read synchronously by technical hackathon judges alongside ~30 other &lt;code&gt;#presagechallenge&lt;/code&gt; posts. Here is what the research across your past posts, the Week 4 Overall Winner, and the strongest live &lt;code&gt;#presagechallenge&lt;/code&gt; entries shows.&lt;/p&gt;


&lt;h3 id="agent-session-1410-23-1-your-own-track-record-why-ghost-visitors-won-week-4-while-strollerpulse--slipsledger-didnt"&gt;1. Your Own Track Record: Why &lt;em&gt;Ghost Visitors&lt;/em&gt; Won Week 4 While &lt;em&gt;StrollerPulse&lt;/em&gt; &amp;amp; &lt;em&gt;SlipsLedger&lt;/em&gt; Didn't&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Compare your own DEV posts side by side:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="table-wrapper-paragraph"&gt;&lt;table&gt;
&lt;thead&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;th&gt;Post&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;th&gt;Voice &amp;amp; Opening&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;th&gt;How Technical Depth Is Shown&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;th&gt;Outcome&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;/thead&gt;
&lt;tbody&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;StrollerPulse&lt;/strong&gt; (Week 1) &amp;amp; &lt;strong&gt;SlipsLedger&lt;/strong&gt; (Week 2)&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Formal product-brochure tone (&lt;em&gt;"is a modern full-stack application..."&lt;/em&gt;, &lt;em&gt;"In line with our engineering ethics..."&lt;/em&gt;), bolded bullet lists, textbook jargon.&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Dense feature lists and formal formulas before the reader feels the problem.&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Did not win&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Ghost Visitors&lt;/strong&gt; (Week 4 — &lt;strong&gt;Winner, Best Use of GitHub Copilot&lt;/strong&gt;)&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Human story in 4 short sentences (&lt;em&gt;"Every website has visitors who leave without saying why. Marisol tried to order on the bus..."&lt;/em&gt;), plain English, punchy rule (&lt;em&gt;"Gemma speaks, code checks."&lt;/em&gt;).&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;A 4-row table (&lt;strong&gt;Run 1 → Run 4&lt;/strong&gt;) + three concrete failure stories (&lt;em&gt;"Marisol found a bug I didn't plant"&lt;/em&gt;, &lt;em&gt;"The guard had a bug too"&lt;/em&gt;, &lt;em&gt;"Tomás couldn't hear"&lt;/em&gt;).&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Won&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Òjà&lt;/strong&gt; (MLH Solana) &amp;amp; &lt;strong&gt;A flow can't wake a flow&lt;/strong&gt; (GitLab)&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Immediate human hook (&lt;em&gt;"Market traders in Lagos sell all day..."&lt;/em&gt;, &lt;em&gt;"A flow can't wake a flow."&lt;/em&gt;), short paragraphs, zero fluff, clean tables (`Attempt \&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Rejected with`).&lt;/td&gt;
