&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;/tbody&gt;
&lt;/table&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Right now, our &lt;strong&gt;AFTERIMAGE&lt;/strong&gt; draft opens like &lt;em&gt;SlipsLedger&lt;/em&gt;:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;blockquote&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;"&lt;/em&gt;&lt;em&gt;AFTERIMAGE&lt;/em&gt;* is a five-scene interactive visual essay navigated without touching a keyboard, powered by real-time facial and respiratory signals from the &lt;strong&gt;Presage SmartSpectra Node.js SDK (&lt;code&gt;@smartspectra/node-sdk@3.5.0&lt;/code&gt;)&lt;/strong&gt;."*&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/blockquote&gt;

&lt;p&gt;And its technical section is an 8-item wall of 100-word bolded bullets instead of the crisp &lt;strong&gt;"Run 1 broke → here is what the numbers showed → here is Run 2"&lt;/strong&gt; arc that made &lt;em&gt;Ghost Visitors&lt;/em&gt; win.&lt;/p&gt;


&lt;h3 id="agent-session-1410-23-2-what-the-top-competitors-in-presagechallenge-are-doing-right-now"&gt;2. What the Top Competitors in &lt;code&gt;#presagechallenge&lt;/code&gt; Are Doing Right Now&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;p&gt;I pulled and read all current &lt;code&gt;#presagechallenge&lt;/code&gt; submissions. Almost two-thirds are generic wellness dashboards, break timers, or wrappers, which won't place. Your real competition for the 10 prizes comes from &lt;strong&gt;five specific entries&lt;/strong&gt; (two of them by fellow Hacktoberfest Week 4 winners):&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ol&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;&lt;a href="https://dev.to/timothy_akanbi/long-exposure-a-daguerreotype-that-takes-a-minute-because-the-sdk-does-113l"&gt;Long Exposure: a daguerreotype that takes a minute, because the SDK does&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/strong&gt; (&lt;code&gt;timothy_akanbi&lt;/code&gt;)

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Why it's dangerous:&lt;/strong&gt; It also uses a darkroom / photographic plate metaphor, opens with a killer line (&lt;em&gt;"In 1840 a portrait took a minute. You had to hold still. Your heart could not."&lt;/em&gt;), has an animated GIF at the top, and uses a crisp table mapping the SDK's 60-second warmup to exposure stages.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Where AFTERIMAGE beats it technically (if we highlight it clearly):&lt;/strong&gt; Look at what &lt;code&gt;timothy_akanbi&lt;/code&gt; admits at the end of &lt;em&gt;Long Exposure&lt;/em&gt;:
&amp;gt; &lt;em&gt;"What I'd do next: Blinks that reliably leave ghost eyes. The SDK's blink flag was too sparse in my sittings, and the face landmarks were too coarse to detect blinks myself."&lt;/em&gt;
You &lt;strong&gt;actually solved&lt;/strong&gt; what he gave up on—because you discovered the 478 landmarks are in raw pixel coordinates (&lt;code&gt;[316..564, 10..350]&lt;/code&gt;), normalized 6-point EAR by local eye-corner span against a &lt;code&gt;0.298–0.313&lt;/code&gt; baseline, and triggered cuts on eyelid &lt;strong&gt;reopen&lt;/strong&gt; (&lt;code&gt;&amp;lt; 650 ms&lt;/code&gt;). Plus, &lt;em&gt;Long Exposure&lt;/em&gt; is a passive 60-second sitting; &lt;em&gt;AFTERIMAGE&lt;/em&gt; is an active 5-scene narrative you steer with blinks, L/C/R gaze, and chest breath.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;&lt;a href="https://dev.to/samarth_kumble_a91ad88634/practical-a-webcam-physiology-lab-that-grades-itself-against-a-wrist-count-3adp"&gt;Practical: a webcam physiology lab that grades itself against a wrist count&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/strong&gt; (&lt;code&gt;samarth_kumble&lt;/code&gt;, Week 4 Winner)

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Why it's strong:&lt;/strong&gt; Opens with a real measurement (&lt;em&gt;"The camera said 70.4. My friend, counting my wrist pulse with a stopwatch, said 70."&lt;/em&gt;), tells the story of how his first version lied (&lt;code&gt;62.5&lt;/code&gt; vs &lt;code&gt;78&lt;/code&gt;), and backs it with a real participant table (&lt;code&gt;P02–P07&lt;/code&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;&lt;a href="https://dev.to/tushar_shah/preppulse-a-pressure-map-for-exam-practice-built-on-smartspectra-265g"&gt;PrepPulse: a pressure map for exam practice, built on SmartSpectra&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/strong&gt; (&lt;code&gt;tushar_shah&lt;/code&gt;, Week 4 Winner)

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Why it's strong:&lt;/strong&gt; Deep real-world grounding (Indian JEE/NEET exam anxiety), 4 live screenshots, and plain-English honesty about what the SDK did and didn't return (e.g., HRV returning zero readings on a live webcam).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;&lt;a href="https://dev.to/emediongrgb/witness-camera-vitals-that-show-their-work-1b73"&gt;Witness: camera vitals that show their work&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/strong&gt; (&lt;code&gt;emediongrgb&lt;/code&gt;)

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Why it's strong:&lt;/strong&gt; Sharp thesis ("Clean-Window Gate" that withholds contaminated readings and issues hash-chained evidence receipts).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Its weakness:&lt;/strong&gt; The author openly admits his laptop webcam couldn't hit 25 fps (&lt;code&gt;kSustainedLowFrameRate&lt;/code&gt;), so he never completed a single live webcam sitting—only pre-recorded phone clips. You have a real &lt;code&gt;205.5 s&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;366&lt;/code&gt;-keyframe live Windows webcam sitting bundled right in the app.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;&lt;a href="https://dev.to/dunoil/firefly-cove-a-night-garden-that-breathes-with-you-3e92"&gt;Firefly Cove, a night garden that breathes with you&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/strong&gt; (&lt;code&gt;dunoil&lt;/code&gt;)

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Why it's strong:&lt;/strong&gt; Clean ambient concept (pulse = fireflies, breath = mist), shows both the consent gate screenshot and the live HUD screenshot.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ol&gt;

&lt;p&gt;And compare all of those to the &lt;strong&gt;Hacktoberfest Week 4 Overall Winner&lt;/strong&gt; (&lt;a href="https://dev.to/mzee04/i-gave-a-tiny-ai-a-diary-then-switched-off-its-brain-one-night-at-a-time-229n"&gt;I gave a tiny AI a diary, then switched off its brain one night at a time&lt;/a&gt; by &lt;code&gt;mzee04&lt;/code&gt;), which won Overall because it &lt;strong&gt;quoted the actual words from the experience&lt;/strong&gt; and paired emotion with hard, reproducible measurements.&lt;/p&gt;


&lt;h3 id="agent-session-1410-23-3-seven-specific-weaknesses-in-our-current-afterimage-draft"&gt;3. Seven Specific Weaknesses in Our Current &lt;code&gt;AFTERIMAGE&lt;/code&gt; Draft&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;ol&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;The title and opening sound like a spec sheet, not &lt;em&gt;Ghost Visitors&lt;/em&gt; or &lt;em&gt;Death Diary&lt;/em&gt;.&lt;/strong&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Current title: &lt;code&gt;"AFTERIMAGE: Steering a Five-Scene Memory Essay with Blinks, Gaze &amp;amp; Chest Breath"&lt;/code&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Notice how every winner (including yours) uses a concrete tension or hook in the title and first three lines:

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;em&gt;Ghost Visitors: the people who left your website come back to haunt it&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;em&gt;Òjà: credit that repays itself, inside one Solana instruction&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;em&gt;In 1840 a portrait took a minute. You had to hold still. Your heart could not.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;We should open directly with Walter Murch's observation (a blink is where the mind cuts a thought, and breathing sets the tempo between cuts) and the exact moment in a sitting where you blink too early (&lt;code&gt;&amp;lt; 4.2 s&lt;/code&gt;), see the shutter ripple refuse the cut, steady your chest breath past &lt;code&gt;60%&lt;/code&gt;, and watch the haze lift off the plate.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;You never quote a single line of the five scenes.&lt;/strong&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;In &lt;em&gt;Ghost Visitors&lt;/em&gt;, you quoted Tomás's epitaph. In &lt;em&gt;Death Diary&lt;/em&gt;, &lt;code&gt;mzee04&lt;/code&gt; quoted the diary entries.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;In our draft, we call it a "five-scene memory essay" and list the five plate titles, &lt;strong&gt;but we never quote what is actually on the page&lt;/strong&gt; or show how looking Left vs. Center vs. Right changes the caption and how holding &lt;code&gt;≥ 60%&lt;/code&gt; breath steadiness reveals the hidden italic marginalia.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;You have a real "Sitting 1 Failed → Sitting 2 Fixed" story (with screenshots of both!) and we buried it inside 8 long bullets.&lt;/strong&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Just like &lt;em&gt;Ghost Visitors&lt;/em&gt; showed the broken bakery (&lt;code&gt;report.png&lt;/code&gt;) vs. the fixed bakery (&lt;code&gt;whispers.png&lt;/code&gt;) and the 4-run table, we have &lt;strong&gt;two real Contact Sheet prints&lt;/strong&gt; from your own face today:

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Sitting 1 (before our fixes):&lt;/strong&gt; Breath clarity froze at &lt;code&gt;55%&lt;/code&gt; (&lt;code&gt;TALKING · BREATH HELD&lt;/code&gt;) from a 1-frame startup &lt;code&gt;face.talking&lt;/code&gt; flicker; the UI stuttered from 30 MediaFoundation camera enumerations/sec; and the gaze bar was &lt;strong&gt;100% Center&lt;/strong&gt; on every plate because &lt;code&gt;0.7 * iris + 0.3 * yaw&lt;/code&gt; damped subtle glances across a 14" laptop screen (&lt;code&gt;0.486–0.493&lt;/code&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Sitting 2 (&lt;code&gt;contact-sheet-sample.png&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;205.5 s&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;366&lt;/code&gt; keyframes):&lt;/strong&gt; &lt;code&gt;63%&lt;/code&gt; average breath clarity (&lt;code&gt;85%&lt;/code&gt; peak), &lt;code&gt;15&lt;/code&gt; clean blink cuts on reopen, and a real &lt;strong&gt;&lt;code&gt;91&lt;/code&gt; Left / &lt;code&gt;235&lt;/code&gt; Center / &lt;code&gt;40&lt;/code&gt; Right&lt;/strong&gt; gaze split across the five plates.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Turning that into a &lt;strong&gt;Sitting 1 vs. Sitting 2 table + narrative&lt;/strong&gt; (instead of 8 dense bullets) will make the post read unmistakably like &lt;em&gt;Ghost Visitors&lt;/em&gt;.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;No scannable Signal-to-Behavior Table.&lt;/strong&gt;

