&lt;p&gt;The last test is the important one. It pins the clock to a UTC instant and checks that we get Riyadh wall-clock time, whatever zone your laptop or CI server is in.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


  5. Server-side fetch with caching (&lt;code&gt;lib/getPrayerTimes.js&lt;/code&gt;)
&lt;/h2&gt;



&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight javascript"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="c1"&gt;// lib/getPrayerTimes.js — runs on the server only&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="no"&gt;SOURCE&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s2"&gt;"https://sunnahsource.org/data/json/prayer-times.json"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="k"&gt;export&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;async&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kd"&gt;function&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;getPrayerTimes&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
