&lt;p&gt;The build output shows the route as static with a 1 h revalidate:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight plaintext"&gt;&lt;code&gt;Route (app)          Size   First Load JS  Revalidate
┌ ○ /             1.23 kB          104 kB          1h
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;Open &lt;code&gt;http://localhost:3000&lt;/code&gt;. The server HTML already has the full timetable (good for SEO and slow phones). After hydration the countdown line switches from "Loading…" to something like &lt;strong&gt;"Next: maghrib in 3h 12m"&lt;/strong&gt;, and that row is highlighted.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


  9. Going further
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Real cities.&lt;/strong&gt; With an API key from the &lt;a href="https://sunnahsource.org/apis/prayer-times/" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;Prayer Times API&lt;/a&gt;, make the city a route segment (&lt;code&gt;app/[city]/page.jsx&lt;/code&gt;) and pass it to &lt;code&gt;getPrayerTimes(city)&lt;/code&gt;. Keep the key in an environment variable. It is only read on the server, so it never reaches the browser.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Hijri date header.&lt;/strong&gt; Add the month names from the &lt;a href="https://sunnahsource.org/apis/hijri-calendar/" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;Hijri Calendar API&lt;/a&gt; sample (&lt;code&gt;/data/json/hijri-calendar.json&lt;/code&gt;, with &lt;code&gt;months[].name_en&lt;/code&gt; / &lt;code&gt;name_ar&lt;/code&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;After-prayer adhkar.&lt;/strong&gt; Link each prayer row to the after-prayer adhkar from the &lt;a href="https://sunnahsource.org/apis/azkar/" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;Azkar API&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Day rollover.&lt;/strong&gt; After Isha the widget shows tomorrow's Fajr using today's time. That is close enough for a widget. For exact times, fetch tomorrow's timetable from the full API.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

