&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;GitHub: &lt;a href="https://github.com/sunnahsourceofficial-droid/sunnahsource-islamic-api" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;https://github.com/sunnahsourceofficial-droid/sunnahsource-islamic-api&lt;/a&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;p&gt;If you build something with it, share it in the comments.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;I download movies, software and project files on my PC, and then I need them on my phone. Every time it was the same story: search for the data cable, or upload the file somewhere and download it again, wasting both time and mobile data. One night I urgently needed a large file on my phone, and the cable was nowhere to be found. That night I decided this problem has to end.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;So my friend Sadhin Khan and I built OurDrop. We are both CSE students at First Capital University of Bangladesh, Chuadanga, and we built it for our own daily use first.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


  &lt;strong&gt;What OurDrop does&lt;/strong&gt;
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;OurDrop moves files of any type and size between a Windows PC and an Android phone, with no internet, no login, no cables, and no cloud. You scan a QR code once, then drag and drop files in both directions.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;It works over your own Wi-Fi, and it also &lt;strong&gt;works over a phone hotspot,&lt;/strong&gt; so no router is needed. That matters a lot here, because in labs and hostels a router is not always available.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;A movie downloaded on my PC reaches my phone in seconds. Photos and videos from my phone go straight to my PC. No cable, no internet cost, no waiting.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


  &lt;strong&gt;How it works&lt;/strong&gt;
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Large files travel in chunks, with pause and resume, and every transfer is verified with SHA-256. If the connection drops in the middle, the transfer resumes instead of starting over.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The phone keeps receiving in the background, even with the app closed, through an Android foreground service. The PC app lives in the system tray and can start with Windows, so the server is ready when you need it.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;In the latest version, you can also share straight to OurDrop from the Gallery or any app's Share menu. The shared files wait if the PC is not connected yet, and they send automatically once it connects.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Both apps update themselves from inside the app, so nobody has to hunt for a new download link.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


  &lt;strong&gt;How we built it&lt;/strong&gt;
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;We started with a small Python prototype. Then we rebuilt it properly, and that rebuild became the app people use today.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The PC app is React and TypeScript for the interface, with a dependency-free Node.js server doing the actual file transfer, wrapped in Electron and packaged with NSIS. The Android app uses the same React interface, with native Java handling the Android work: background receiving, Wi-Fi and hotspot checks, and the share target.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;It took more than 60 versions to get here. We tested every version on my own phone and PC, broke it many times, and fixed it again. We presented it in our university lab on Friday, 20 November 2026, and we still use it every day at home.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;This project taught me more about real software than any tutorial ever did, because real users, including ourselves, find the problems no tutorial mentions.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


  &lt;strong&gt;What is next&lt;/strong&gt;
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;OurDrop is now public and open source under the MIT license. The code and the latest downloads are on GitHub.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;We are still improving it. One thing we learned from real use is that many desktop PCs have no Wi-Fi at all, only a cable, so we are thinking about how to connect in those places too.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;If you try it, tell us what breaks. Feedback, bug reports and GitHub stars are most welcome.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Thank you, Sadhin Khan, for building this with me.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


  &lt;strong&gt;Try it or see the code:&lt;/strong&gt;
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;GitHub: &lt;a href="https://github.com/Ali-Emam-Rabbi/OurDrop-Software-Project" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;https://github.com/Ali-Emam-Rabbi/OurDrop-Software-Project&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Download (latest version): &lt;a href="https://github.com/Ali-Emam-Rabbi/OurDrop-Software-Project/releases" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;https://github.com/Ali-Emam-Rabbi/OurDrop-Software-Project/releases&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The PR adds Zustand so a settings modal can keep an &lt;code&gt;open&lt;/code&gt; flag. The repo already uses Redux (or Recoil, or a single React context plus React Query) for app state, and local &lt;code&gt;useState&lt;/code&gt; for UI that does not need to be global. The new dependency is a second source of truth, a second devtools path, and a new pattern for the next agent to copy.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;I’ve started treating &lt;strong&gt;a new state library in a feature PR as a scope break&lt;/strong&gt;, even if the modal works. One widget is not a reason to change how the app holds state.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


  Why the extra library shows up
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Many training examples reach for Zustand or Redux Toolkit as the default. The model will not audit &lt;code&gt;package.json&lt;/code&gt; unless you say “we already have X; do not add Y.” A modal’s &lt;code&gt;open&lt;/code&gt; flag also does not need a store at all.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;You pay twice: bundle size, and a review surface where some flows go through the existing store and others go through the new one.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


  A simple state-library policy
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Use the existing state approach&lt;/strong&gt; (the current store, server cache, or local state)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Do not add Zustand, Redux, Jotai, Valtio, or a new context framework&lt;/strong&gt; in a feature PR&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;UI-only state stays local&lt;/strong&gt; unless something distant already needs to read it&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;A migration off the current library is its own PR&lt;/strong&gt;, with a plan, not a side effect of a modal&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;p&gt;If the existing store is painful for this case, say that in the PR. Do not quietly start a second one.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


  What to put in the prompt
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight plaintext"&gt;&lt;code&gt;Do not add a new state-management library.
Use the existing store/helpers in src/store (or local useState) for this UI.
A modal open flag should be local state unless another route already needs it.
If the current store cannot express this, stop and explain; do not install a second library.
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Paste &lt;code&gt;package.json&lt;/code&gt; dependencies and one existing store usage. In review, search the diff for new packages (&lt;code&gt;zustand&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;jotai&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;recoil&lt;/code&gt;, a second Redux wrapper) and for a new &lt;code&gt;createStore&lt;/code&gt; / &lt;code&gt;createContext&lt;/code&gt; used only by the new widget.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


  Reject / send back
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Reject&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A new state library added for one component&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Global store state for a purely local &lt;code&gt;open&lt;/code&gt; / &lt;code&gt;tab&lt;/code&gt; flag&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A second context “provider layer” that duplicates the existing store&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A partial migration that leaves both libraries in the tree&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Accept&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Local state for widget-only UI&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A change that goes through the existing store or server cache&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A dedicated RFC or migration PR, not mixed into a feature&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;p&gt;React Router is the standard way to add multiple pages to a React app. Without it, your app is one long page. With it, &lt;code&gt;/home&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;/about&lt;/code&gt;, and &lt;code&gt;/profile&lt;/code&gt; become real URLs the user can bookmark, share, and navigate with the back button.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Setup is simple:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight shell"&gt;&lt;code&gt;npm install react-router-dom
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;





&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight jsx"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="k"&gt;import&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nc"&gt;BrowserRouter&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nc"&gt;Routes&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nc"&gt;Route&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nc"&gt;Link&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;from&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s2"&gt;"react-router-dom"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="kd"&gt;function&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nc"&gt;App&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="k"&gt;return&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;BrowserRouter&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
      &lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;nav&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
        &lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;Link&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;to&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;"/"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;Home&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;Link&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
        &lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;Link&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;to&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;"/about"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;About&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;Link&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
      &lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;nav&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
      &lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;Routes&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
        &lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;Route&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;path&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;"/"&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;element&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;Home&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;/&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;/&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
        &lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;Route&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;path&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;"/about"&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;element&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;About&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;/&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;/&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
        &lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;Route&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;path&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;"/users/:id"&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;element&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;UserProfile&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;/&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;/&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
      &lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;Routes&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;BrowserRouter&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;Dynamic routes use &lt;code&gt;:id&lt;/code&gt; in the path. Inside the component, read it with a hook:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight jsx"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="k"&gt;import&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;useParams&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;from&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s2"&gt;"react-router-dom"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="kd"&gt;function&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nc"&gt;UserProfile&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;id&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;useParams&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="k"&gt;return&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;h1&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;Profile&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;of&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;user&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;id&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;h1&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;Navigation in code uses &lt;code&gt;useNavigate&lt;/code&gt; — for example, sending the user to a dashboard after login:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight jsx"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="k"&gt;import&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;useNavigate&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;from&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s2"&gt;"react-router-dom"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;navigate&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;useNavigate&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nf"&gt;navigate&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;"/dashboard"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;Nested routes let you build layouts once and reuse them. A dashboard layout with a sidebar stays in place while only the inner content changes between pages — that is how most real apps are structured.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Who is it for? Anyone building a React app with more than one screen. It is basically required for dashboards, blogs, shops, and anything with user accounts.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The limits: it only handles client-side routing, so SEO for public pages needs extra work like server-side rendering. And if your app is a single screen, adding a router is unnecessary complexity.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Start today: add two routes and one dynamic route to a practice project, plus a link between them. That is the whole core of routing — everything else is built on top of it.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Recoil is a state management library for React made by Facebook. It solves a specific problem: sharing state between components without prop drilling and without the boilerplate of Redux. If you have ever passed props through four components just to reach one button, Recoil is worth learning.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The two core ideas are atoms and selectors. An atom is a single piece of state:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight jsx"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="k"&gt;import&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;atom&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;useRecoilState&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;from&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s2"&gt;"recoil"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;countState&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;atom&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="n"&gt;key&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s2"&gt;"countState"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="k"&gt;default&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="mi"&gt;0&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="kd"&gt;function&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nc"&gt;Counter&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;[&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;count&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;setCount&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;]&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;useRecoilState&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;countState&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="k"&gt;return&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;button&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;onClick&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;setCount&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;count&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;+&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="mi"&gt;1&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;count&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;button&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;Any component can read or update that atom, no matter where it sits in the tree. You just wrap your app in &lt;code&gt;RecoilRoot&lt;/code&gt; once:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight jsx"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="k"&gt;import&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nc"&gt;RecoilRoot&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;from&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s2"&gt;"recoil"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;RecoilRoot&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;App&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;/&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;RecoilRoot&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;Selectors are derived state — values computed from atoms, like a filtered list:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight jsx"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="k"&gt;import&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;selector&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;useRecoilValue&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;from&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s2"&gt;"recoil"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;doubledState&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;selector&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="n"&gt;key&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s2"&gt;"doubledState"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="n"&gt;get&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;get&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;get&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;countState&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;*&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="mi"&gt;2&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;doubled&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;useRecoilValue&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;doubledState&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;Only components that use a particular atom re-render when it changes. That is the big win over Context, where one value change can re-render everything below the provider.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Who is it for? React developers whose apps have outgrown &lt;code&gt;useState&lt;/code&gt; and prop drilling but do not need Redux. Small to medium apps with shared state — theme, user data, filters, carts — are the sweet spot.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The limits: Recoil is still officially experimental in some senses, and its community is smaller than Redux or Zustand. There is no built-in devtools as polished as Redux DevTools. And for very large apps with complex async logic, you may still want something heavier.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Start today: take one piece of state you currently pass through three or more components and move it into an atom. If the code gets shorter and clearer, Recoil has earned its place in your project.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Ant Design, often called antd, is one of the most complete React component libraries out there. It was built for enterprise dashboards and admin panels, which means it has components other libraries do not even attempt: data tables with sorting and pagination, date pickers, forms with validation, trees, and transfer lists. If you are building a data-heavy app, antd saves you weeks.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Installation is straightforward:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight shell"&gt;&lt;code&gt;npm install antd
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;





&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight jsx"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="k"&gt;import&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nc"&gt;Button&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nc"&gt;Table&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nc"&gt;DatePicker&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;from&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s2"&gt;"antd"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;columns&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;[&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;title&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s2"&gt;"Name"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;dataIndex&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s2"&gt;"name"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;key&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s2"&gt;"name"&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;title&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s2"&gt;"Age"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;dataIndex&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s2"&gt;"age"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;key&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s2"&gt;"age"&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;title&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s2"&gt;"City"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;dataIndex&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s2"&gt;"city"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;key&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s2"&gt;"city"&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;]&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;data&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;[&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;key&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s2"&gt;"1"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;name&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s2"&gt;"Aarav"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;age&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="mi"&gt;24&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;city&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s2"&gt;"Delhi"&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;key&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s2"&gt;"2"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;name&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s2"&gt;"Meera"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;age&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="mi"&gt;29&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;city&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s2"&gt;"Mumbai"&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;]&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="kd"&gt;function&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nc"&gt;App&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="k"&gt;return&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
      &lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;DatePicker&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;/&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
      &lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;Button&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kd"&gt;type&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;"primary"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;Add&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;user&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;Button&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
      &lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;Table&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;columns&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;columns&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;dataSource&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;data&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;/&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;/&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;That table already sorts, paginates, and looks professional. Building the same thing by hand would take a day.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The form system is where antd really shines. Validation rules, error messages, and layout are all declared in one place:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight jsx"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;Form&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;onFinish&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;values&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nb"&gt;console&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;log&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;values&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;Form&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;Item&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="n"&gt;name&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;"email"&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="n"&gt;label&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;"Email"&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="n"&gt;rules&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;[&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;required&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kc"&gt;true&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kd"&gt;type&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s2"&gt;"email"&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;]&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;Input&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;/&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;Form&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;Item&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;Button&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kd"&gt;type&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;"primary"&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;htmlType&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;"submit"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;Submit&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;Button&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;Form&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;Who is it for? Developers building admin panels, dashboards, and internal tools — the kind of apps with lots of tables and forms. If your app is mostly data in and data out, antd is hard to beat.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The trade-offs: the default design looks corporate and is hard to make playful or unique. The bundle is large, so it is not a great pick for a tiny marketing page. And the API surface is huge, so expect to keep the docs open while you learn it.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Start today: build a small table of dummy data with sorting and a form with one validated field. That one exercise will show you why teams pick antd for serious apps.&lt;/p&gt;
